258
00:08:54,981 --> 00:08:58,632
♪ I love Ken he is my sweet friend ♪

259
00:08:58,632 --> 00:09:00,592
- You always tell me,
"Bear it like a man."

260
00:09:00,592 --> 00:09:02,664
- Ah, come on, Dan, your
problem is you're jealous!

261
00:09:02,664 --> 00:09:03,765
(laughing)
(Joel laughs mockingly)

262
00:09:03,765 --> 00:09:05,355
- That's rich.
- Quit teasing.

263
00:09:05,355 --> 00:09:07,576
- Okay.
- Yeah, terrific.

264
00:09:07,576 --> 00:09:10,685
♪ I love Ken, he is my sweet friend ♪

265
00:09:10,685 --> 00:09:12,058
♪ And I love Ken ♪
- Cut it out.

266
00:09:12,058 --> 00:09:14,117
- There's something peculiar about him.

267
00:09:14,117 --> 00:09:14,978
- [Joel] Mm-hmm!

268
00:09:14,978 --> 00:09:16,637
That's good blow, mm-hmm!

269
00:09:16,637 --> 00:09:19,815
- [Man] Top experts in
advanced defense technology.

270
00:09:19,815 --> 00:09:20,975
- You heard right.
- Uh-huh.

271
00:09:20,975 --> 00:09:22,085
- [Man] And you probably know all about

272
00:09:22,085 --> 00:09:24,986
that secret weapon Caysar is said to have

273
00:09:24,986 --> 00:09:26,885
imported from another planet.

274
00:09:26,885 --> 00:09:28,365
- [Tom] Pretty much.

275
00:09:28,365 --> 00:09:30,783
- There any truth to
those rumors, Colonel?

276
00:09:30,783 --> 00:09:32,192
- [Dan] They say it could
blow up the universe.

277
00:09:32,192 --> 00:09:33,461
- [Tom] Or worse!

278
00:09:33,461 --> 00:09:34,703
- Where did you hear that?

279
00:09:34,703 --> 00:09:36,815
- (chuckling) Well,
you know, occasionally,

280
00:09:36,815 --> 00:09:39,445
I tune into the intergalactic grapevine.

281
00:09:39,445 --> 00:09:40,463
(laughing)
(mock laughing)

282
00:09:40,463 --> 00:09:41,349
- Captain Joe--

283
00:09:41,349 --> 00:09:42,213
- [Joel] Shut up.

284
00:09:42,213 --> 00:09:43,130
- I take it

285
00:09:43,965 --> 00:09:45,823
you're trying to enlist my cooperation

286
00:09:45,823 --> 00:09:47,165
for a mission you're about to--

287
00:09:47,165 --> 00:09:48,714
(Joel and bots grunt)

288
00:09:48,714 --> 00:09:50,965
Before I say yes or no,

289
00:09:50,965 --> 00:09:53,152
I'll need to know more
about your intentions.

290
00:09:53,152 --> 00:09:55,042
- [Rocky] I'll love you
all the days of my life.

291
00:09:55,042 --> 00:09:56,431
- I don't know whatever gave you the idea

292
00:09:56,431 --> 00:09:58,034
we're planning a mission.

293
00:09:58,034 --> 00:09:59,634
We're just out for a ride.

294
00:09:59,634 --> 00:10:01,342
A little excursion to discover more facts

295
00:10:01,342 --> 00:10:02,434
about our universe.

296
00:10:02,434 --> 00:10:03,392
(Joel chuckles)

297
00:10:03,392 --> 00:10:04,943
- You don't say.

298
00:10:04,943 --> 00:10:06,973
And how do I know I can trust you?

299
00:10:06,973 --> 00:10:10,245
This Ken fellow seems
mighty suspicious to me.

300
00:10:10,245 --> 00:10:13,016
- (chuckles) Ken's just a bit of a loner.

301
00:10:13,016 --> 00:10:13,947
If you want, I'll call him in,

302
00:10:13,947 --> 00:10:15,456
and you can talk to himself.

303
00:10:15,456 --> 00:10:16,289
- Ken's a loaner?

304
00:10:16,289 --> 00:10:17,893
How long before your Ken is fixed?

305
00:10:17,893 --> 00:10:18,726
(Tom chuckles)

306
00:10:18,726 --> 00:10:19,704
- [Joe] Ken?

307
00:10:19,704 --> 00:10:20,537
Tammy?

308
00:10:21,503 --> 00:10:22,336
I want to see you.

309
00:10:22,336 --> 00:10:25,587
- [Joel] Oh, great, he
found out about the keg.

310
00:10:25,587 --> 00:10:27,816
- [Tom] Plot point right there.

311
00:10:27,816 --> 00:10:28,864
Hm?

312
00:10:28,864 --> 00:10:30,523
- This is a girl officer's insignia.

313
00:10:30,523 --> 00:10:31,356
- [Tom] Say.

314
00:10:31,356 --> 00:10:32,560
- How did you get it?

315
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:35,400
- Through a lot of hard work
and a lot of pancake makeup.

316
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:37,052
- When you were sleeping,

317
00:10:37,052 --> 00:10:38,972
I heard you call a girl's name out loud.

318
00:10:38,972 --> 00:10:40,321
- [Tom] When I put your
hand in warm water.

319
00:10:40,321 --> 00:10:41,654
- Rita, I think.

320
00:10:42,561 --> 00:10:43,982
I believe that was it.

321
00:10:43,982 --> 00:10:45,753
Does the name Rita mean anything to you?

322
00:10:45,753 --> 00:10:47,930
- [Joel] Uh, it's a Beatles song?

323
00:10:47,930 --> 00:10:48,763
- Ken!

324
00:10:50,062 --> 00:10:51,473
- [Rocky] This is our present position.

325
00:10:51,473 --> 00:10:53,806
Pegasus R2, IS4, right here.

326
00:10:54,671 --> 00:10:55,871
- Here's the Spencer Gifts.

327
00:10:55,871 --> 00:10:58,033
- Distance to Saysar is a rollatime.

328
00:10:58,033 --> 00:10:59,191
- [Joel] A rolla-who?

329
00:10:59,191 --> 00:11:00,024
- [Tom] Rolodex.

330
00:11:00,024 --> 00:11:02,241
- Two-one-three, sir.

331
00:11:02,241 --> 00:11:04,382
- Course three-seven is perfectly safe.

332
00:11:04,382 --> 00:11:06,131
It's when we switch to course T

333
00:11:06,131 --> 00:11:08,620
that we're likely to run into trouble.

334
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:11,004
There's a huge black hole
near R-five-by-nine--

335
00:11:11,004 --> 00:11:14,111
- [Joel] And a vicious
dog laying to the left.

336
00:11:14,111 --> 00:11:16,338
- Black hole, huh?
- Oh, neat.

337
00:11:16,338 --> 00:11:18,738
- It swallows up anything that
comes up anywhere near it.

338
00:11:18,738 --> 00:11:22,175
(Joel mimics scrubbing)
I don't think we can risk it.

339
00:11:22,175 --> 00:11:24,602
- [Tom] Oh look, another
painting by Judy Chicago.

340
00:11:24,602 --> 00:11:26,124
Now back to our movie.

341
00:11:26,124 --> 00:11:28,615
- This puts a new light on
the conditions of our mission.

342
00:11:28,615 --> 00:11:29,594
- A black light.

343
00:11:29,594 --> 00:11:31,935
- The odds against success
are extremely high.

344
00:11:31,935 --> 00:11:34,023
- [Tom] But then, I'm
extremely high. (chuckles)

345
00:11:34,023 --> 00:11:35,793
- On the other hand, if we've gotta go,

346
00:11:35,793 --> 00:11:37,674
I can't think of a better way.
- Huh?

347
00:11:37,674 --> 00:11:38,775
- That's not funny, sir.

348
00:11:38,775 --> 00:11:39,912
- I'll say it isn't.

349
00:11:39,912 --> 00:11:41,924
I don't want to vanish in thin air.

350
00:11:41,924 --> 00:11:44,775
When my time comes, I
want to go out in glory.

351
00:11:44,775 --> 00:11:45,883
- [Joel] I want to be
torn apart my animals!

352
00:11:45,883 --> 00:11:48,155
- Spoken like a true
woman, and a naive one.

353
00:11:48,155 --> 00:11:49,235
- Naive yourself!

354
00:11:49,235 --> 00:11:50,068
- Me so silly!

355
00:11:50,068 --> 00:11:51,044
(laughing)

356
00:11:51,044 --> 00:11:52,825
- Captain Joe, you don't necessarily

357
00:11:52,825 --> 00:11:54,915
have to get swallowed up in a black hole.

358
00:11:54,915 --> 00:11:56,085
- [Tom] But it helps.

359
00:11:56,085 --> 00:11:57,685
- If you chart your course carefully,

360
00:11:57,685 --> 00:11:59,095
you can go through a tunnel

361
00:11:59,095 --> 00:12:01,605
out to a white hole and safety.

362
00:12:01,605 --> 00:12:03,415
It's a tricky maneuver.

363
00:12:03,415 --> 00:12:04,248
- [Tom] Turkey?

364
00:12:04,248 --> 00:12:05,754
- Where did you hear that?

365
00:12:05,754 --> 00:12:06,983
- Where did I hear it?

366
00:12:06,983 --> 00:12:08,503
I'm afraid I don't remember.

367
00:12:08,503 --> 00:12:09,485
I guess it was at one of those

368
00:12:09,485 --> 00:12:11,354
scientific briefings I attended.

369
00:12:11,354 --> 00:12:15,354
- [Joel] Yeah, at my
aunt's house or somethin'.

370
00:12:16,834 --> 00:12:17,943
- [Colonel] Ken, wait!

371
00:12:17,943 --> 00:12:19,274
- You're walking down someone's throat!

372
00:12:19,274 --> 00:12:20,853
(Colonel chuckles)

373
00:12:20,853 --> 00:12:23,262
- [Joel] Wait a second, I
didn't tell you the punchline.

374
00:12:23,262 --> 00:12:24,534
- Little slip of the tongue and you gave

375
00:12:24,534 --> 00:12:26,382
your whole game away, didn't you?

376
00:12:26,382 --> 00:12:28,270
- Yup.
- I don't understand.

377
00:12:28,270 --> 00:12:29,361
- Do you find me pleasing?

378
00:12:29,361 --> 00:12:32,359
- I know for a fact that only
a handful of Wolf attackers

379
00:12:32,359 --> 00:12:34,349
have ever made it through a black hole

380
00:12:34,349 --> 00:12:36,937
and still lived to tell the tale.

381
00:12:36,937 --> 00:12:38,470
I only had to put two and two together

382
00:12:38,470 --> 00:12:40,239
to realize you're a Star Wolf.

383
00:12:40,239 --> 00:12:42,378
- [Tom] Who are you to judge?

384
00:12:42,378 --> 00:12:43,211
Huh?
(Colonel grunts)

385
00:12:43,211 --> 00:12:47,075
- Don't be a fool, Ken, I'm the
only friend you've got here!

386
00:12:47,075 --> 00:12:49,843
(grunts)

387
00:12:49,843 --> 00:12:50,784
- What's up?

388
00:12:50,784 --> 00:12:52,544
What's going on?

389
00:12:52,544 --> 00:12:54,995
- It's all my fault.

390
00:12:54,995 --> 00:12:55,835
- [Tom] Yeah, he was just showing him

391
00:12:55,835 --> 00:12:57,883
where his larynx was.

392
00:12:57,883 --> 00:13:01,803
- I foolishly made a sarcastic
remark about earthlings.

393
00:13:01,803 --> 00:13:04,315
Ken was right to act as he did.

394
00:13:04,315 --> 00:13:06,683
Ill-chosen words have
been known to start wars.

395
00:13:06,683 --> 00:13:09,155
- Yeah, the Sarcasm Wars of 1999.

396
00:13:09,155 --> 00:13:10,772
- [Joel And Tom] Mm.
(Colonel chuckles)

397
00:13:10,772 --> 00:13:12,883
- What a dipstick.

398
00:13:12,883 --> 00:13:15,123
- I don't like that guy.

399
00:13:15,123 --> 00:13:16,945
And I don't like you, either.

400
00:13:16,945 --> 00:13:18,065
- [Ken] The feeling is mutual, Rocky.

401
00:13:18,065 --> 00:13:19,798
- [Tom] Oh, Rocky, who do you like?

402
00:13:19,798 --> 00:13:20,857
- [Dan] Captain!

403
00:13:20,857 --> 00:13:23,198
Come up here, quick!

404
00:13:23,198 --> 00:13:24,435
- Here he comes.
- Surprise!

405
00:13:24,435 --> 00:13:26,075
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

406
00:13:26,075 --> 00:13:26,974
- Look at that, sir.

407
00:13:26,974 --> 00:13:28,134
What do you make of it?

408
00:13:28,134 --> 00:13:29,734
- Ah, it's one of those nut clusters.

409
00:13:29,734 --> 00:13:31,227
- [Rocky] Looks like a meteorite.

410
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:32,060
Quite a big one.

411
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:33,336
- Yeah, just one thing's wrong,

412
00:13:33,336 --> 00:13:35,566
I don't see it on any chart.

413
00:13:35,566 --> 00:13:36,904
- [Rocky] By the time
they get it on the chart,

414
00:13:36,904 --> 00:13:38,185
it'll probably have broken up.

415
00:13:38,185 --> 00:13:39,505
- [Joel] Like most rock bands, huh?

416
00:13:39,505 --> 00:13:40,454
- [Tom] Oh, good one.
(Crow laughs)

417
00:13:40,454 --> 00:13:41,353
- [Joel] Yeah, I speak the truth.

418
00:13:41,353 --> 00:13:42,273
- You bet.
- Amen.

419
00:13:42,273 --> 00:13:44,992
- Looks like we're getting
into hostile territory.

420
00:13:44,992 --> 00:13:46,583
We have to be on our guard.

421
00:13:46,583 --> 00:13:47,643
Rocky, take the controls.

422
00:13:47,643 --> 00:13:49,383
- Again?
- Hurry, back to your station.

423
00:13:49,383 --> 00:13:50,216
- [Rocky] Yes, sir.

424
00:13:50,216 --> 00:13:51,049
- [Tom] Rocky, you hate Ken,

425
00:13:51,049 --> 00:13:52,273
Ken, you make goofy faces,

426
00:13:52,273 --> 00:13:53,493
Tammy, you love Rocky.

427
00:13:53,493 --> 00:13:54,682
Uh, or Ken.

428
00:13:54,682 --> 00:13:57,103
- Colonel Yurulin, that's your seat there.

429
00:13:57,103 --> 00:13:58,884
- But, Captain--
- He said sit down.

430
00:13:58,884 --> 00:14:00,513
- [Joel] But he didn't say Simon says!

431
00:14:00,513 --> 00:14:02,164
- [Tom] He said Captain says.

432
00:14:02,164 --> 00:14:03,215
Oh, wait a minute, which is moving?

433
00:14:03,215 --> 00:14:04,823
The stars or the ship?

434
00:14:04,823 --> 00:14:06,564
- Um, the stars?

435
00:14:06,564 --> 00:14:08,423
- [Joel] Pink Floyd on the headphones,

436
00:14:08,423 --> 00:14:12,052
set the controls for the heart of the sun.

437
00:14:12,052 --> 00:14:13,442
- It's broccoli!

438
00:14:13,442 --> 00:14:15,463
I hate broccoli.

439
00:14:15,463 --> 00:14:17,874
- [Joel] You know, he's
got Kristy McNichol cheeks,

440
00:14:17,874 --> 00:14:18,863
you know, when you look at him?

441
00:14:18,863 --> 00:14:21,063
- I don't like this at all.

442
00:14:21,063 --> 00:14:22,263
- Ken.
- Yes, sir.

443
00:14:22,263 --> 00:14:24,604
- Destroy the meteorite
with the forward laser.

444
00:14:24,604 --> 00:14:25,437
- Okay!

445
00:14:25,437 --> 00:14:26,506
- Yes, sir!

446
00:14:26,506 --> 00:14:27,714
(zapping)

447
00:14:27,714 --> 00:14:29,404
♪ Love, love, love ♪

448
00:14:29,404 --> 00:14:32,487
(upbeat theme music)

449
00:14:35,714 --> 00:14:37,674
- Captain Joe, we're still alive!

450
00:14:37,674 --> 00:14:39,219
That's the only thing that counts.

451
00:14:39,219 --> 00:14:42,042
- [Joel] No, cleanliness is
the only thing that counts!

452
00:14:42,042 --> 00:14:43,562
- I won't feel safe while he's alive.

453
00:14:43,562 --> 00:14:44,450
- Kill him.

454
00:14:44,450 --> 00:14:45,517
- What do you think you're doing?

455
00:14:45,517 --> 00:14:47,117
- We've got a mission to accomplish.

456
00:14:47,117 --> 00:14:48,577
I'm just going to remove an obstacle.

457
00:14:48,577 --> 00:14:50,538
- [Joel] Your eyebrow.

458
00:14:50,538 --> 00:14:51,919
- Ken, stop him!

459
00:14:51,919 --> 00:14:53,629
If he kills me, you're next!

460
00:14:53,629 --> 00:14:54,901
- [Ken] Easy, Rocky.

461
00:14:54,901 --> 00:14:55,821
This isn't the right moment.

462
00:14:55,821 --> 00:14:56,848
- Out of my way.

463
00:14:56,848 --> 00:14:57,850
- Rocky, hold your fire.

464
00:14:57,850 --> 00:14:58,762
- Again?

465
00:14:58,762 --> 00:15:00,301
- I'm sorry to say we still need him.

466
00:15:00,301 --> 00:15:01,930
- Need him for what?

467
00:15:01,930 --> 00:15:04,669
- We rescued him to guide us
to Saysar and he'll do it.

468
00:15:04,669 --> 00:15:06,250
Lock him up.

469
00:15:06,250 --> 00:15:08,050
- Rack 'em up.
- Whatever you say.

470
00:15:08,050 --> 00:15:10,568
- I just hope you know what you're doing.

471
00:15:10,568 --> 00:15:13,199
- [Tom] I just want to
say your makeup sucks.

472
00:15:13,199 --> 00:15:14,959
- As long as this guy's traveling with us,

473
00:15:14,959 --> 00:15:16,549
our mission is threatened.

474
00:15:16,549 --> 00:15:18,638
- [Joel] We'll never make it to Woodstock!

475
00:15:18,638 --> 00:15:19,511
- [Tom] Huh? Huh?

476
00:15:19,511 --> 00:15:20,434
- Huh?
- Huh?

477
00:15:20,434 --> 00:15:21,267
- Huh?
- Huh?

478
00:15:21,267 --> 00:15:22,842
- Oh, well.
- Huh?

479
00:15:22,842 --> 00:15:25,808
- Hey, hey, ho, ho!
- Huh-huh-huh-ho!

480
00:15:25,808 --> 00:15:30,808
(grunts)
(Joel and bots growl)

481
00:15:32,050 --> 00:15:33,399
- Well, here you are.

482
00:15:33,399 --> 00:15:35,889
It isn't the royal suite,
but it'll just have to do.

483
00:15:35,889 --> 00:15:37,309
- [Tom] You want room service, dial nine.

484
00:15:37,309 --> 00:15:39,040
There's a mint on the pillow.

485
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:39,949
- I need some towels!

486
00:15:39,949 --> 00:15:41,248
- Listen to me!

487
00:15:41,248 --> 00:15:42,840
If you want to make it
to Saysar in one piece,

488
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:44,770
you need me to guide you!

489
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:47,469
Any minute now we'll be
going by Demeter star.

490
00:15:47,469 --> 00:15:49,069
It'll set us on fire!

491
00:15:49,069 --> 00:15:50,728
Let me out, let me out!

492
00:15:50,728 --> 00:15:52,570
- [Joel] I'm gonna hold my
breath till I turn blue!

493
00:15:52,570 --> 00:15:53,592
Oh, I'm already,

494
00:15:53,592 --> 00:15:56,151
oh, I did it again, I'm already blue.

495
00:15:56,151 --> 00:15:59,522
- [Tom] Zinged yourself there. (chuckles)

496
00:15:59,522 --> 00:16:00,355
(Tom hums)

497
00:16:00,355 --> 00:16:01,512
(grunting)
- Huh?

498
00:16:01,512 --> 00:16:04,520
- [Tom] Diarrhea is like
a storm raging inside you.

499
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:06,741
(groans)

500
00:16:06,741 --> 00:16:07,970
- [Joel] I'm comin', Elizabeth!

501
00:16:07,970 --> 00:16:08,900
- [Tom] Ooh!

502
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:10,754
- He's hallucinating split ends.

503
00:16:10,754 --> 00:16:13,602
(Tom sings along with score)

504
00:16:13,602 --> 00:16:14,602
- [Tom] Huh?

505
00:16:16,234 --> 00:16:17,813
Oh, (chuckles) who am I tryin' to kid?

506
00:16:17,813 --> 00:16:19,144
I'm not sick.

507
00:16:19,144 --> 00:16:24,144
(ship whooshes)
(Crow mimics whooshing)

508
00:16:24,522 --> 00:16:26,682
- [Joel] Mm-hmm, that's good amyl!

509
00:16:26,682 --> 00:16:27,515
Ho, ho!

510
00:16:27,515 --> 00:16:28,522
- What's the cabin temperature?

511
00:16:28,522 --> 00:16:31,104
- [Tom] It's hotter than
my great aunt's apartment.

512
00:16:31,104 --> 00:16:32,522
- 26.
- Tenperature?

513
00:16:32,522 --> 00:16:33,360
(Tom chuckles)

514
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:35,053
- That seems a bit high.

515
00:16:35,053 --> 00:16:36,824
- [Joel] Sunny side? Of the street?

516
00:16:36,824 --> 00:16:39,372
- It's even hotter outside.

517
00:16:39,372 --> 00:16:41,709
- (grunts) That calls for a drink.

518
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:42,981
- I'll go check it out.

519
00:16:42,981 --> 00:16:44,061
- Ken.
- Huh?

520
00:16:44,061 --> 00:16:45,394
- Wait a minute.

521
00:16:47,450 --> 00:16:48,500
Look at that star.

522
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:49,560
- You look at that. I'm bitter.

523
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:53,053
(foreboding music)

524
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:54,002
- I don't get it.

525
00:16:54,002 --> 00:16:55,912
That star, why, that's Demeter star.

526
00:16:55,912 --> 00:16:57,701
- [Tom] Oh, it should
be bigger than a meter.

527
00:16:57,701 --> 00:16:58,721
- How'd we get here?

528
00:16:58,721 --> 00:17:00,791
It isn't on our course.

529
00:17:00,791 --> 00:17:01,708
- [Tom] Hm.

530
00:17:03,242 --> 00:17:04,075
Hm.

531
00:17:05,621 --> 00:17:08,613
- Look at this, we're just drifting, sir!

532
00:17:08,613 --> 00:17:12,000
Saysar isn't anywhere near here!

533
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,181
- Wow.

534
00:17:13,181 --> 00:17:14,659
- We'll have to correct our course.

535
00:17:14,659 --> 00:17:16,139
Switch over to seven-three-oh.

536
00:17:16,139 --> 00:17:17,820
- Oh, what is that, traffic information?

537
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:18,800
(Tom chuckles)

538
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:20,381
(grunting)

539
00:17:20,381 --> 00:17:21,214
- It won't move!

540
00:17:21,214 --> 00:17:22,047
There's something wrong!

541
00:17:22,047 --> 00:17:24,289
- [Tom] Yeah, it's this
movie, it sucks. (chuckles)

542
00:17:24,289 --> 00:17:26,840
- [Ken] We must be caught
in Demeter's magnetic field!

543
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:29,368
All the controls are blocked!

544
00:17:29,368 --> 00:17:32,312
(growling)

545
00:17:32,312 --> 00:17:33,479
- [Tom] Uh-oh.

546
00:17:34,729 --> 00:17:36,341
- [Joel] Man, if it's not
one thing, it's another.

547
00:17:36,341 --> 00:17:38,200
Honey, I'm gonna be very late.

548
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,541
- [Joe] I've gotta see you right away.

549
00:17:39,541 --> 00:17:40,880
It's an emergency.

550
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:42,781
- Again?
- Rocky?

551
00:17:42,781 --> 00:17:43,821
- [Tom] He shouldn't spend too much time

552
00:17:43,821 --> 00:17:45,602
away from the bathroom.
(groaning)

553
00:17:45,602 --> 00:17:47,050
(grunting)

554
00:17:47,050 --> 00:17:50,442
- [Joel] Oh, could you Armorall my suit?

555
00:17:50,442 --> 00:17:51,780
- Rocky.
- Again?

556
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:53,113
- Rocky!
- Again?

557
00:17:54,588 --> 00:17:56,051
- [Tom] (chuckles) That's good, Crow.

558
00:17:56,051 --> 00:17:57,305
(beeping)
- Captain!

559
00:17:57,305 --> 00:17:59,687
- I scored another game!
- We're back to normal!

560
00:17:59,687 --> 00:18:01,577
- All engines at full thrust.

561
00:18:01,577 --> 00:18:03,410
- Engines full thrust!

562
00:18:04,487 --> 00:18:05,596
- [Joel] That's full thrust?

563
00:18:05,596 --> 00:18:07,057
- Yeah, big deal.
- Lame.

564
00:18:07,057 --> 00:18:08,358
- [Tom] What luck, huh?

565
00:18:08,358 --> 00:18:10,526
- [Joel] Looks like an aerosol can.

566
00:18:10,526 --> 00:18:12,038
- I don't feel right about this at all.

567
00:18:12,038 --> 00:18:13,086
- [Crow] You and me both, pal.

568
00:18:13,086 --> 00:18:13,998
You and me both.

569
00:18:13,998 --> 00:18:16,246
- Something suspicious.

570
00:18:16,246 --> 00:18:17,596
We'd better get out of here

571
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:18,678
or be roasted alive.

572
00:18:18,678 --> 00:18:19,595
- [Tom] Ah.

573
00:18:21,529 --> 00:18:22,362
Huh?

574
00:18:22,362 --> 00:18:23,198
Oh, Rocky, no.

575
00:18:23,198 --> 00:18:24,427
On the paper, boy!

576
00:18:24,427 --> 00:18:25,318
Come on.

577
00:18:25,318 --> 00:18:26,940
- It was the salmon mousse.

578
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:28,600
(bots grunting)

579
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:29,510
- [Joe] Rocky, what's wrong?

580
00:18:29,510 --> 00:18:31,259
- [Joel] Oh, Rocky cubed it.

581
00:18:31,259 --> 00:18:32,219
(grunting)

582
00:18:32,219 --> 00:18:34,193
- Pants too tight!

583
00:18:34,193 --> 00:18:35,188
I'm--

584
00:18:35,188 --> 00:18:36,551
- Sir.
- Turning Japanese!

585
00:18:36,551 --> 00:18:38,130
- I've got this pain in my back.

586
00:18:38,130 --> 00:18:39,703
- [Tom] I really think so.

587
00:18:39,703 --> 00:18:41,361
- My--
- What?

588
00:18:41,361 --> 00:18:42,881
- Rocky.
- I'm feeling dizzy!

589
00:18:42,881 --> 00:18:43,972
- [Joe] Ken, take over.

590
00:18:43,972 --> 00:18:44,889
- Yes, sir.

591
00:18:46,391 --> 00:18:48,244
- Captain!
- Ooh!

592
00:18:48,244 --> 00:18:49,473
- [Tom] She's looked better, hasn't she?

593
00:18:49,473 --> 00:18:50,772
(chuckles)

594
00:18:50,772 --> 00:18:51,673
- Tammy, it's all right.

595
00:18:51,673 --> 00:18:53,423
- [Tammy] Captain, help me!

596
00:18:53,423 --> 00:18:55,553
- [Joel] Oh, come on, you
kids are just overtired.

597
00:18:55,553 --> 00:18:56,531
You're fighting sleep.

598
00:18:56,531 --> 00:18:58,382
Now I want you to go to bed.
(Tom mimics crying)

599
00:18:58,382 --> 00:18:59,799
Come on, come on.

600
00:19:01,291 --> 00:19:02,412
- Those are just the after effects

601
00:19:02,412 --> 00:19:03,591
of the ultra high speed we needed

602
00:19:03,591 --> 00:19:05,017
to get through the black hole.

603
00:19:05,017 --> 00:19:06,340
You'll just have to sleep it off.

604
00:19:06,340 --> 00:19:08,130
I'll get you some medication.

605
00:19:08,130 --> 00:19:09,201
- For me, too, sir.

606
00:19:09,201 --> 00:19:10,188
- [Tom] All right, me, too!

607
00:19:10,188 --> 00:19:11,559
- For me, too, sir.
- This'll relieve the pain.

608
00:19:11,559 --> 00:19:13,119
- Take it.

609
00:19:13,119 --> 00:19:14,137
- [Rocky] Sir?

610
00:19:14,137 --> 00:19:15,449
- [Joe] Yeah?

611
00:19:15,449 --> 00:19:17,957
- Are you sure you'll be all right?

612
00:19:17,957 --> 00:19:19,977
You went through the black hole, too.

613
00:19:19,977 --> 00:19:22,396
- [Joel] I'll be fine, I got
my friend Jack to help me.

614
00:19:22,396 --> 00:19:24,552
(Tom chuckles)
What, is he in an automat?

615
00:19:24,552 --> 00:19:26,192
- It looks like it.
- Check it out.

616
00:19:26,192 --> 00:19:27,963
- [Tom] Oh, chicken salad,
grab me a chick sal.

617
00:19:27,963 --> 00:19:29,392
- What's the matter?

618
00:19:29,392 --> 00:19:31,163
Can't anyone hear me?

619
00:19:31,163 --> 00:19:32,246
- [Tom] Sure.

620
00:19:34,822 --> 00:19:36,392
- It's so hot.

621
00:19:36,392 --> 00:19:37,686
Where is all this heat coming from?

622
00:19:37,686 --> 00:19:39,184
- [Tom] No, you see, it's not
the heat, it's the humidity.

623
00:19:39,184 --> 00:19:40,136
You see, the comfort index says--

624
00:19:40,136 --> 00:19:41,344
- Listen to me!

625
00:19:41,344 --> 00:19:43,235
I've got something important to tell you!

626
00:19:43,235 --> 00:19:46,914
- [Joel] I'm the unsinkable Molly Brown!

627
00:19:46,914 --> 00:19:49,616
- [Tom] Think they could
make bigger doors. (chuckles)

628
00:19:49,616 --> 00:19:51,784
- Well, sir, how are they doing?

629
00:19:51,784 --> 00:19:52,617
- Okay.

630
00:19:52,617 --> 00:19:54,646
I gave them something to calm them down.

631
00:19:54,646 --> 00:19:56,456
They're just gonna have to sleep it off.

632
00:19:56,456 --> 00:19:58,539
- [Joel] I do that a lot.

633
00:20:00,946 --> 00:20:02,947
(groans)

634
00:20:02,947 --> 00:20:04,478
- Still awfully hot in here.

635
00:20:04,478 --> 00:20:06,216
- Yeah, turn up the AC.
- I know.

636
00:20:06,216 --> 00:20:08,216
- Captain, we really ought to move away

637
00:20:08,216 --> 00:20:10,027
as quickly as we can.

638
00:20:10,027 --> 00:20:11,665
I think we oughta boost to the engines.

639
00:20:11,665 --> 00:20:12,798
- Hm.
- Hm.

640
00:20:12,798 --> 00:20:15,643
- [Tom] Nothin'.
(engines bang)

641
00:20:15,643 --> 00:20:16,476
(beeps)

642
00:20:16,476 --> 00:20:18,283
- [Joel] Uh, curly fries are up, sir!

643
00:20:18,283 --> 00:20:21,064
(dramatic, worrying music)

644
00:20:21,064 --> 00:20:23,442
- [Tom] Hm? Well, at least
they spelled speed right.

645
00:20:23,442 --> 00:20:24,992
(Tom chuckles)

646
00:20:24,992 --> 00:20:26,282
- Engine trouble.

647
00:20:26,282 --> 00:20:27,733
- [Tom] Ah, I told you to check the oil.

648
00:20:27,733 --> 00:20:29,882
Didn't we fill it up in Auclair?

649
00:20:29,882 --> 00:20:31,965
- Okay, I'll take her up.

650
00:20:32,893 --> 00:20:36,123
- Those daring young men
in their jaunty jalopies!

651
00:20:36,123 --> 00:20:38,322
(Tom sings along with music)

652
00:20:38,322 --> 00:20:39,733
- [Joel] What is with you, sir?

653
00:20:39,733 --> 00:20:41,253
Did you eat those radishes again?

654
00:20:41,253 --> 00:20:44,264
- Captain, what's the matter?

655
00:20:44,264 --> 00:20:45,264
- [Tom] Huh?

656
00:20:46,372 --> 00:20:47,562
- [Ken] Dan, wake up!

657
00:20:47,562 --> 00:20:49,123
- [Tom] Wake up, you're
late for cram school!

658
00:20:49,123 --> 00:20:51,325
- Rocky, Rocky!
- Again?

659
00:20:51,325 --> 00:20:52,536
- You gotta wake up!

660
00:20:52,536 --> 00:20:53,845
You gotta wake up!

661
00:20:53,845 --> 00:20:54,678
Rocky!

662
00:20:54,678 --> 00:20:59,195
- [Tom] Ah, jeez, he's been
reading Bukowski again.

663
00:20:59,195 --> 00:21:01,100
- Let me out of here!
- Hm?

664
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:02,910
- [Yurulin] Let me out of here!

665
00:21:02,910 --> 00:21:03,876
- [Joel] Oh, phooey.

666
00:21:03,876 --> 00:21:05,734
- [Tom] Wah, wah, wah.

667
00:21:05,734 --> 00:21:08,234
- We have no time for you now!

668
00:21:09,607 --> 00:21:11,476
You just stay in here and
stop all that yelling.

669
00:21:11,476 --> 00:21:12,788
- Yeah, you'll just have to hold it.

670
00:21:12,788 --> 00:21:14,708
- Haven't you noticed this heat?

671
00:21:14,708 --> 00:21:15,988
What's causing it?

672
00:21:15,988 --> 00:21:17,428
I want to know exactly where we are.

673
00:21:17,428 --> 00:21:19,047
- Enough of your questions!

674
00:21:19,047 --> 00:21:19,988
Be quiet.

675
00:21:19,988 --> 00:21:21,727
I'll just have to get back to you later.

676
00:21:21,727 --> 00:21:22,738
- [Crow] Bye!

677
00:21:22,738 --> 00:21:24,218
- Listen to me!

678
00:21:24,218 --> 00:21:25,396
Pay attention!

679
00:21:25,396 --> 00:21:26,695
We mustn't get near Demeter star!

680
00:21:26,695 --> 00:21:27,628
- Why not?

681
00:21:27,628 --> 00:21:29,527
This heat's coming from the engines.

682
00:21:29,527 --> 00:21:30,418
- You little fool.

683
00:21:30,418 --> 00:21:31,548
- You little minx!

684
00:21:31,548 --> 00:21:34,727
- Don't you realize the Demeter
star is about to explode?

685
00:21:34,727 --> 00:21:35,566
- What's that?

686
00:21:35,566 --> 00:21:36,716
- [Joel] Really?

687
00:21:36,716 --> 00:21:37,847
He never said anything about--

688
00:21:37,847 --> 00:21:40,748
- [Tom] Oh, looks like
Captain Joe is drunk again.

689
00:21:40,748 --> 00:21:42,287
For those of you playing along at home,

690
00:21:42,287 --> 00:21:44,607
in Fugitive Alien I,
Captain Joe was portrayed

691
00:21:44,607 --> 00:21:46,468
as quite the drinkin' man. (chuckles)

692
00:21:46,468 --> 00:21:47,776
Now this.

693
00:21:47,776 --> 00:21:49,367
(groans)
- [Joel] Ooh.

694
00:21:49,367 --> 00:21:52,160
- [Tom] I kinda feel like
him of all of a sudden.

695
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:53,649
(Joe groans)
No, I'll be okay, I'm fine.

696
00:21:53,649 --> 00:21:57,521
(coughs) Something I ate, I think.

697
00:21:57,521 --> 00:21:58,640
- [Joe] Ahh.

698
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,473
(door opens)

699
00:21:59,473 --> 00:22:01,192
(Tom bubbles)

700
00:22:01,192 --> 00:22:02,508
- Captain!
- Focus. Focus!

701
00:22:02,508 --> 00:22:03,982
- [Rocky] Help me get him off the floor.

702
00:22:03,982 --> 00:22:05,313
(groans)

703
00:22:05,313 --> 00:22:06,500
- [Tom] Ah, oh.

704
00:22:06,500 --> 00:22:08,241
Could you wipe my brow?

705
00:22:08,241 --> 00:22:10,510
- [Joel] You don't look
very good, you know?

706
00:22:10,510 --> 00:22:12,329
- [Tom] My left arm is a
little numb, I don't know.

707
00:22:12,329 --> 00:22:13,849
- Guess it must have been a--

708
00:22:13,849 --> 00:22:14,682
- [Tom] Ah, I'm fine.

709
00:22:14,682 --> 00:22:16,470
Ah, so (clears throat)--
- High speed.

710
00:22:16,470 --> 00:22:18,079
- Captain!
- What's going on here?

711
00:22:18,079 --> 00:22:19,012
- Yurulin?

712
00:22:19,012 --> 00:22:20,420
Who let you out?

713
00:22:20,420 --> 00:22:21,790
- Captain listen to me!

714
00:22:21,790 --> 00:22:22,790
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

715
00:22:22,790 --> 00:22:24,612
- You don't realize what's going on!

716
00:22:24,612 --> 00:22:25,909
This sort of heat is only generated

717
00:22:25,909 --> 00:22:27,332
by a star that's about to die.

718
00:22:27,332 --> 00:22:28,559
That's what's happening to Demeter,

719
00:22:28,559 --> 00:22:29,990
and we've gotta get out of here!

720
00:22:29,990 --> 00:22:31,809
- Oh.
- What's that?

721
00:22:31,809 --> 00:22:33,478
- And it'll explode?

722
00:22:33,478 --> 00:22:35,660
Listen, Ken, Colonel Yurulin is the one

723
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:36,998
who knows his way around here.

724
00:22:36,998 --> 00:22:38,606
We're going to have to enlist his help.

725
00:22:38,606 --> 00:22:40,438
(Tom groans)
- Okay, sir.

726
00:22:40,438 --> 00:22:41,568
- Captain!
- Oh.

727
00:22:41,568 --> 00:22:42,457
- First we must find out--

728
00:22:42,457 --> 00:22:43,487
- [Tom] I'm a little woozy, guys.

729
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:44,508
- All right.
- Oh, boy.

730
00:22:44,508 --> 00:22:45,710
- [Joe] I have no choice.

731
00:22:45,710 --> 00:22:48,030
- [Tom] I'm feelin' really bad. (chuckles)

732
00:22:48,030 --> 00:22:49,121
- [Rocky] Ken, let's go!

733
00:22:49,121 --> 00:22:51,239
- [Tom] Oh, boy, I feel
like I'm just sinkin' off

734
00:22:51,239 --> 00:22:53,041
a spooky drunk--

735
00:22:53,041 --> 00:22:53,982
(grunts)
(shattering)

736
00:22:53,982 --> 00:22:57,124
- [Joel] Tom! Tom Servo,
what happened, buddy?

737
00:22:57,124 --> 00:22:57,957
- It's all over the seat!

738
00:22:57,957 --> 00:22:59,444
- We gotta get him outta here!

739
00:22:59,444 --> 00:23:00,611
Come on, Crow!

740
00:23:08,533 --> 00:23:09,744
Tom Servo!
(ambulance siren blares)

741
00:23:09,744 --> 00:23:10,713
Oh, my God!

742
00:23:10,713 --> 00:23:12,525
Tom Servo's dead!

743
00:23:12,525 --> 00:23:14,632
He's dying, it must have been that movie!

744
00:23:14,632 --> 00:23:17,052
Oh, man, we're losing him!

745
00:23:17,052 --> 00:23:18,693
- A robot watches a bad film.

746
00:23:18,693 --> 00:23:20,115
It renders him unconscious.

747
00:23:20,115 --> 00:23:22,172
Next on Emergency 911.

748
00:23:22,172 --> 00:23:25,253
- Crow, you gotta snap out
of Shatner and help me!

749
00:23:25,253 --> 00:23:28,155
It means the life of our friend Tom Servo!

750
00:23:28,155 --> 00:23:30,053
- But I must finish TekWars of Venusia,

751
00:23:30,053 --> 00:23:31,293
must direct Star Trek IX,

752
00:23:31,293 --> 00:23:33,283
The Search for Spock's Intelligence,

753
00:23:33,283 --> 00:23:34,343
Hooker's a good cop!

754
00:23:34,343 --> 00:23:35,653
Oh, he's a good, oh--

755
00:23:35,653 --> 00:23:37,715
- Crow, you listen to
me and you listen good!

756
00:23:37,715 --> 00:23:39,253
I need you to snap out of Shatner!

757
00:23:39,253 --> 00:23:40,873
I need you here now!
(sobbing)

758
00:23:40,873 --> 00:23:43,413
Our friend's life hangs
hangs in the balance!

759
00:23:43,413 --> 00:23:45,885
- I'm sorry, Joel, I didn't know!

760
00:23:45,885 --> 00:23:47,803
- I know, man, I know.

761
00:23:47,803 --> 00:23:49,381
But we gotta get our little buddy

762
00:23:49,381 --> 00:23:51,416
out of the bone orchard, okay?

763
00:23:51,416 --> 00:23:54,356
Listen, I need you to run along
and get the defibrillator,

764
00:23:54,356 --> 00:23:56,176
and I'm gonna try to get our brother Tommy

765
00:23:56,176 --> 00:23:57,485
out of the Badlands.

766
00:23:57,485 --> 00:23:58,376
- [Crow] Okay, all right.

767
00:23:58,376 --> 00:23:59,565
- Come on, man.

768
00:23:59,565 --> 00:24:03,154
Come on back, we're all
pullin' for ya, buddy! (sobs)

769
00:24:03,154 --> 00:24:04,653
- [Crow] Hey, Joel, is the defibrillator

770
00:24:04,653 --> 00:24:06,805
the thing that looks like a vacuum cleaner

771
00:24:06,805 --> 00:24:09,093
or a thing that looks
