(chuckles)

1028
00:32:33,493 --> 00:32:34,493
- Thank you.

1029
00:32:35,506 --> 00:32:36,866
- Ken?
- Get outta my seat.

1030
00:32:36,866 --> 00:32:38,306
- Colonel Yurulin.

1031
00:32:38,306 --> 00:32:41,746
You know, both did a terrific job.

1032
00:32:41,746 --> 00:32:43,405
I won't forget it.

1033
00:32:43,405 --> 00:32:45,364
- This old crate pulled
us through one more time.

1034
00:32:45,364 --> 00:32:46,327
(Tom chuckles)

1035
00:32:46,327 --> 00:32:49,077
- [Joel] You're cute, both of ya.

1036
00:32:50,685 --> 00:32:52,154
- [Ken] Thanks again, Bacchus 3.

1037
00:32:52,154 --> 00:32:53,586
- Bacchus! (chuckles)
- Good job!

1038
00:32:53,586 --> 00:32:57,826
- [Tom] Now you've done
it again. (chuckles)

1039
00:32:57,826 --> 00:32:59,135
- [Joel and Crow] Mighty Jack!

1040
00:32:59,135 --> 00:33:00,424
- [Joel] Yeah.

1041
00:33:00,424 --> 00:33:02,091
- [Tom] Mighty Jack?

1042
00:33:03,375 --> 00:33:04,426
- [Joel] I'm quite a guy, really.

1043
00:33:04,426 --> 00:33:05,259
You know?

1044
00:33:09,495 --> 00:33:10,405
- [Tom] So?

1045
00:33:10,405 --> 00:33:11,775
- Hey, Dan, come on.

1046
00:33:11,775 --> 00:33:13,114
- We're goin' fishin'.
- Rise and shine.

1047
00:33:13,114 --> 00:33:14,525
- You promised.
- How you doin'?

1048
00:33:14,525 --> 00:33:15,466
- [Dan] Still a little groggy.

1049
00:33:15,466 --> 00:33:16,299
- [Tammy] Is everybody all right?

1050
00:33:16,299 --> 00:33:17,586
- Not too bad.

1051
00:33:17,586 --> 00:33:18,914
- I feel great.

1052
00:33:18,914 --> 00:33:19,994
Ready for a workout!

1053
00:33:19,994 --> 00:33:21,493
- [Joel] Yeah, you got spunk.

1054
00:33:21,493 --> 00:33:23,370
I hate spunk.

1055
00:33:23,370 --> 00:33:24,649
- What is it?

1056
00:33:24,649 --> 00:33:26,112
- [Ken] This is your morning call, sir.

1057
00:33:26,112 --> 00:33:27,632
We'll be expecting you all downstairs

1058
00:33:27,632 --> 00:33:29,040
in an hour for some tennis.

1059
00:33:29,040 --> 00:33:30,560
- [Tom] Is this the Morning Zoo guys?

1060
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:32,330
- Okay, I'll go string my racket.

1061
00:33:32,330 --> 00:33:34,461
Say, what happened to room service?

1062
00:33:34,461 --> 00:33:35,610
- [Ken] Sorry, sir.

1063
00:33:35,610 --> 00:33:38,373
I'm afraid our guests have
to cook their own breakfast.

1064
00:33:38,373 --> 00:33:40,162
- [Joel] Enough with the
good-natured ribbing.

1065
00:33:40,162 --> 00:33:41,521
Bye!
- You bet!

1066
00:33:41,521 --> 00:33:42,420
- [Tom] I love it.

1067
00:33:42,420 --> 00:33:45,503
(upbeat theme music)

1068
00:33:48,896 --> 00:33:51,449
- [Man] Please hold your
present position for the moment.

1069
00:33:51,449 --> 00:33:54,171
We'll be giving you your
landing instructions shortly.

1070
00:33:54,171 --> 00:33:55,004
- Shortly?

1071
00:33:56,211 --> 00:33:57,670
What's the delay?

1072
00:33:57,670 --> 00:34:01,190
- They may have to clear a
landing space for us, that's all.

1073
00:34:01,190 --> 00:34:03,249
Message received, we're
holding our position

1074
00:34:03,249 --> 00:34:04,299
and waiting to hear from you.

1075
00:34:04,299 --> 00:34:06,110
- [Joel] All our best
to Joan and the kids.

1076
00:34:06,110 --> 00:34:09,193
(engines power down)

1077
00:34:10,379 --> 00:34:13,019
- [Tom] So looks like I'll
just, uh, park there then.

1078
00:34:13,019 --> 00:34:13,979
- Oh.

1079
00:34:13,979 --> 00:34:15,067
- [Tom] Park in the street, it'll be okay.

1080
00:34:15,067 --> 00:34:17,447
- I think I could speed things
up if I had a word with them.

1081
00:34:17,447 --> 00:34:19,339
- Oh, Mr. Connections.

1082
00:34:19,339 --> 00:34:21,357
- [Tom] Oh, Mr. Sarcasm.

1083
00:34:21,357 --> 00:34:24,238
- Colonel Yurulin calling
Saysar Headquarters.

1084
00:34:24,238 --> 00:34:25,099
- [Man] Yurulin?

1085
00:34:25,099 --> 00:34:26,089
- Yup, we're number one!

1086
00:34:26,089 --> 00:34:28,108
- The Earth Space Command
was kind enough to rescue me

1087
00:34:28,108 --> 00:34:29,676
from a Karara prison.

1088
00:34:29,676 --> 00:34:31,996
I can vouch for every one of the crew.

1089
00:34:31,996 --> 00:34:34,294
We'd like to land on Saysar right away.

1090
00:34:34,294 --> 00:34:35,316
- [Joel] Bite me?

1091
00:34:35,316 --> 00:34:36,206
Is that official?

1092
00:34:36,206 --> 00:34:40,908
(radio static crackles)
(worrying music)

1093
00:34:40,908 --> 00:34:42,385
- Say, that's the matter down there?

1094
00:34:42,385 --> 00:34:44,036
I'm used to having my official requests

1095
00:34:44,036 --> 00:34:45,894
dealt with immediately!
- Oh, do you?

1096
00:34:45,894 --> 00:34:47,556
- Did you hear that?

1097
00:34:47,556 --> 00:34:49,073
- [Man] We read you loud and clear.

1098
00:34:49,073 --> 00:34:50,094
- [Joel] We just don't like you.

1099
00:34:50,094 --> 00:34:51,796
- [Man] We have no Colonel Yurulin

1100
00:34:51,796 --> 00:34:53,745
listed on our officers roster.

1101
00:34:53,745 --> 00:34:55,446
- Don't talk nonsense!

1102
00:34:55,446 --> 00:34:57,153
Check that roster again!

1103
00:34:57,153 --> 00:34:59,486
I've been a senior officer
in the Saysar Command

1104
00:34:59,486 --> 00:35:01,566
for the last 20 years!

1105
00:35:01,566 --> 00:35:04,228
Captain, I think there's
some sort of a mistake.

1106
00:35:04,228 --> 00:35:05,518
- [Tom] Starting with the script.

1107
00:35:05,518 --> 00:35:07,809
- Colonel Yurulin, it sounds
like you're pretending

1108
00:35:07,809 --> 00:35:09,609
to be someone you aren't.

1109
00:35:09,609 --> 00:35:10,769
- Nobody asked you!

1110
00:35:10,769 --> 00:35:12,457
This insubordination is unheard of!

1111
00:35:12,457 --> 00:35:14,849
- [Joel] Three week's detention for Ken!

1112
00:35:14,849 --> 00:35:17,158
- Well, you did reveal a
few vital military secrets

1113
00:35:17,158 --> 00:35:19,038
to Karans, didn't ya?

1114
00:35:19,038 --> 00:35:20,008
- Wait a second, you're saying

1115
00:35:20,008 --> 00:35:22,140
I gave away vital information.

1116
00:35:22,140 --> 00:35:23,060
- [Joel] Yeah.

1117
00:35:23,060 --> 00:35:25,249
- How did you find out about that?

1118
00:35:25,249 --> 00:35:26,230
(Joel and bots gulp)

1119
00:35:26,230 --> 00:35:27,238
- By gettin' drunk.

1120
00:35:27,238 --> 00:35:28,761
- Anyway, now it seems we're all involved

1121
00:35:28,761 --> 00:35:30,361
in this situation together.

1122
00:35:30,361 --> 00:35:31,470
- [Tom] Yup.

1123
00:35:31,470 --> 00:35:32,870
- This is no trade mission.

1124
00:35:32,870 --> 00:35:34,451
You're after that secret
weapon, aren't you?

1125
00:35:34,451 --> 00:35:35,284
- Colonel Yurulin--

1126
00:35:35,284 --> 00:35:36,802
- Your mouthwash just ain't makin' it.

1127
00:35:36,802 --> 00:35:39,019
- If we are after it,

1128
00:35:39,019 --> 00:35:40,950
then I think you're the
least likely individual

1129
00:35:40,950 --> 00:35:42,261
to lead us to it.

1130
00:35:42,261 --> 00:35:44,482
They don't even know you down there.

1131
00:35:44,482 --> 00:35:46,219
- It's ridiculous.

1132
00:35:46,219 --> 00:35:47,264
Bunch of idiots!

1133
00:35:47,264 --> 00:35:49,181
- [Tom] Ship of fools!

1134
00:35:49,181 --> 00:35:50,770
- What the heck is goin' on?

1135
00:35:50,770 --> 00:35:52,232
(Tom chuckles)

1136
00:35:52,232 --> 00:35:53,541
- [Tom] Oh, no, no.

1137
00:35:53,541 --> 00:35:55,352
(dramatic music)

1138
00:35:55,352 --> 00:35:57,504
Oh, it's starting over!

1139
00:35:57,504 --> 00:35:58,681
Help!
- Oh, boy.

1140
00:35:58,681 --> 00:35:59,657
- [Tom] I'm gonna bust
it again, let me tell ya.

1141
00:35:59,657 --> 00:36:01,238
- Are they really trying to attack?

1142
00:36:01,238 --> 00:36:03,878
- [Joel] Is she really going out with him?

1143
00:36:03,878 --> 00:36:05,076
- That was just a warning.

1144
00:36:05,076 --> 00:36:06,118
Ken, keep your cool.

1145
00:36:06,118 --> 00:36:07,736
- You're wrong.

1146
00:36:07,736 --> 00:36:09,347
Those guys aren't kidding.

1147
00:36:09,347 --> 00:36:10,809
- I can't believe it!

1148
00:36:10,809 --> 00:36:14,118
My own people would
never dare shoot at me!

1149
00:36:14,118 --> 00:36:15,009
- [Joe] Looks like they have.

1150
00:36:15,009 --> 00:36:16,577
Engines full blast!

1151
00:36:16,577 --> 00:36:17,410
(booms)

1152
00:36:17,410 --> 00:36:18,577
- [Tom] Oh, you know, I just love

1153
00:36:18,577 --> 00:36:22,916
the whole incoherent Mighty
Jack quality of this film.

1154
00:36:22,916 --> 00:36:25,257
(Tom sings along with music)

1155
00:36:25,257 --> 00:36:26,766
(whimpers)

1156
00:36:26,766 --> 00:36:27,926
- Could you repeat that please?

1157
00:36:27,926 --> 00:36:29,956
- [Tom] It was kind of a kuh-ruh-huh.

1158
00:36:29,956 --> 00:36:31,539
- [Joel] I wet 'em.

1159
00:36:33,136 --> 00:36:34,975
- [Tom] This week, join Jonny, Hadgi,

1160
00:36:34,975 --> 00:36:38,588
Race Bannon and Bandit. (barks)

1161
00:36:38,588 --> 00:36:39,798
Jonny Quest.

1162
00:36:39,798 --> 00:36:41,028
- We're surrounded!

1163
00:36:41,028 --> 00:36:44,206
They'll attack again any minute!

1164
00:36:44,206 --> 00:36:46,078
(Tom sings along with music)

1165
00:36:46,078 --> 00:36:48,468
- Don't let insects
spoil your garden party.

1166
00:36:48,468 --> 00:36:49,301
- Captain!

1167
00:36:50,148 --> 00:36:51,417
- [Joel] Pia Zadora?

1168
00:36:51,417 --> 00:36:52,499
No, aw.

1169
00:36:52,499 --> 00:36:53,688
- Ugh.

1170
00:36:53,688 --> 00:36:56,656
- [Tom] Oh no, they're being
attacked by Norelco razors!

1171
00:36:56,656 --> 00:36:58,037
- Even the name says merry Christmas.

1172
00:36:58,037 --> 00:37:01,949
- [Tom] It, uh (sighs)--

1173
00:37:01,949 --> 00:37:03,219
- (grunts) I'm going to get them!

1174
00:37:03,219 --> 00:37:05,856
- [Joel] It's too dark
to go out on your bike!

1175
00:37:05,856 --> 00:37:08,157
- [Tom] Get back here.

1176
00:37:08,157 --> 00:37:10,365
- Don't fire back, try to make contact!

1177
00:37:10,365 --> 00:37:11,465
Tell them it's a mistake!

1178
00:37:11,465 --> 00:37:12,986
- What are you, Captain
Kirk all of a sudden?

1179
00:37:12,986 --> 00:37:14,525
(Tom chuckles)

1180
00:37:14,525 --> 00:37:16,096
- Mistake? This is for real.

1181
00:37:16,096 --> 00:37:18,227
Get ready to counter attack.

1182
00:37:18,227 --> 00:37:19,060
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

1183
00:37:19,060 --> 00:37:22,565
- [Joel] Magic booze bottle, take me away!

1184
00:37:22,565 --> 00:37:26,667
(Tom sings along with music)

1185
00:37:26,667 --> 00:37:27,936
- [Tom] Ole!

1186
00:37:27,936 --> 00:37:30,997
(lasers zap)

1187
00:37:30,997 --> 00:37:32,146
(Tom chuckles)

1188
00:37:32,146 --> 00:37:32,979
Ooh.

1189
00:37:34,324 --> 00:37:35,924
- I got it! (chuckling)

1190
00:37:35,924 --> 00:37:37,244
- Oh, is killing fun, Ken?

1191
00:37:37,244 --> 00:37:39,114
Does it amuse you?

1192
00:37:39,114 --> 00:37:40,164
♪ Let's all watch Ken ♪

1193
00:37:40,164 --> 00:37:42,164
♪ As he tries to kill the badguys ♪

1194
00:37:42,164 --> 00:37:43,825
♪ They'll taste their steel ♪

1195
00:37:43,825 --> 00:37:46,186
♪ Then they'll drink their own blood ♪

1196
00:37:46,186 --> 00:37:50,306
♪ They'll try to kill
him with a forklift ♪

1197
00:37:50,306 --> 00:37:51,194
- [Tom] I'm makin' this up as I go.

1198
00:37:51,194 --> 00:37:54,444
- [Joel] Faster, pussy-Ken, kill, kill.

1199
00:37:58,874 --> 00:37:59,874
- All right, go.

1200
00:37:59,874 --> 00:38:01,804
- [Tom] Like you've never goed before.

1201
00:38:01,804 --> 00:38:02,746
- I'll show 'em.

1202
00:38:02,746 --> 00:38:03,579
- I'll run away!

1203
00:38:03,579 --> 00:38:05,283
Then they'll be sorry they picked on me.

1204
00:38:05,283 --> 00:38:06,572
(mimics childish sobbing)

1205
00:38:06,572 --> 00:38:08,989
(lasers zap)

1206
00:38:10,471 --> 00:38:12,474
Why is Ken behaving like this?

1207
00:38:12,474 --> 00:38:17,057
- [Tom] Because it's bitter
and because it's his heart.

1208
00:38:19,103 --> 00:38:20,143
- [Joel] Bang, bang!

1209
00:38:20,143 --> 00:38:21,602
Killing is fun!

1210
00:38:21,602 --> 00:38:24,019
(lasers zap)

1211
00:38:24,981 --> 00:38:25,943
(explosion booms)

1212
00:38:25,943 --> 00:38:27,711
- Ho, and he picks up the spare!

1213
00:38:27,711 --> 00:38:30,361
- [Tom] Yeah, so let's
review the plot so far.

1214
00:38:30,361 --> 00:38:32,861
They went into outer space, and, uh,

1215
00:38:32,861 --> 00:38:35,101
let's see, uh, oh, wait a minute,

1216
00:38:35,101 --> 00:38:36,951
it's, uh--
- Yeah.

1217
00:38:36,951 --> 00:38:38,023
- [Tom] They went into space and,

1218
00:38:38,023 --> 00:38:38,922
it's on the tip of my tongue.

1219
00:38:38,922 --> 00:38:41,554
- Oh, I know, I know, they,
uh, suffocated for a while--

1220
00:38:41,554 --> 00:38:42,662
- Yeah, yeah.
- And, uh--

1221
00:38:42,662 --> 00:38:45,504
- [Joel] And then I think
came lots of explosions?

1222
00:38:45,504 --> 00:38:48,762
- [Tom] I think a bang,
zoom. (mimics explosions)

1223
00:38:48,762 --> 00:38:50,984
- [Joel] I think that's it.

1224
00:38:50,984 --> 00:38:52,904
- [Tom] That's stuff.

1225
00:38:52,904 --> 00:38:54,881
- Whew! I really enjoyed that.

1226
00:38:54,881 --> 00:38:56,539
- You're sick, buddy.
- Don't get so enthusiastic.

1227
00:38:56,539 --> 00:38:57,748
- Now that they know where we are,

1228
00:38:57,748 --> 00:38:59,030
they're gonna send out the next wave.

1229
00:38:59,030 --> 00:39:01,241
- Well, you know the old
saying, an eye for an eye.

1230
00:39:01,241 --> 00:39:03,459
- Breakfast and tennis! (chuckles)

1231
00:39:03,459 --> 00:39:05,109
- Captain, here they come again!

1232
00:39:05,109 --> 00:39:05,942
- [Tom] Ooh!

1233
00:39:05,942 --> 00:39:06,921
Catch 'em if you can.

1234
00:39:06,921 --> 00:39:07,769
♪ Ooh ♪

1235
00:39:07,769 --> 00:39:09,129
- There's no way out of this, sir.

1236
00:39:09,129 --> 00:39:11,121
Sooner or later, one of
them is gonna score a hit.

1237
00:39:11,121 --> 00:39:11,954
- Off the bong.

1238
00:39:11,954 --> 00:39:13,044
- Colonel Yurulin!
- Woo!

1239
00:39:13,044 --> 00:39:14,177
- [Joe] Can you guide us to a safe place

1240
00:39:14,177 --> 00:39:16,554
to make an emergency landing?

1241
00:39:16,554 --> 00:39:19,115
- Uh, my uncle's got a
planet, let's crash there.

1242
00:39:19,115 --> 00:39:20,446
- Look, if you wanna stay alive,

1243
00:39:20,446 --> 00:39:21,523
you're gonna have to help us.

1244
00:39:21,523 --> 00:39:22,566
Where can we land?

1245
00:39:22,566 --> 00:39:25,086
- Well, I do know of a place.

1246
00:39:25,086 --> 00:39:26,766
- All right.

1247
00:39:26,766 --> 00:39:27,937
Tell us where it is.

1248
00:39:27,937 --> 00:39:30,006
- Everyone calls it the Devil's Desert.

1249
00:39:30,006 --> 00:39:30,897
- [Joel] Sounds pretty neat!

1250
00:39:30,897 --> 00:39:32,275
- If you're really
willing to take the risk,

1251
00:39:32,275 --> 00:39:33,694
I'll be glad to guide you.

1252
00:39:33,694 --> 00:39:35,180
- Okay.

1253
00:39:35,180 --> 00:39:36,013
Let's go!

1254
00:39:36,013 --> 00:39:37,169
- We're goin' to Vegas, everybody!

1255
00:39:37,169 --> 00:39:42,086
(cheering)
(engines boom)

1256
00:39:42,926 --> 00:39:44,676
- [Joel] Looks like the big, blue marble.

1257
00:39:44,676 --> 00:39:46,426
- Sure does.
- Mm-hmm.

1258
00:39:49,634 --> 00:39:50,584
- [Tom] Okay, let's see here.

1259
00:39:50,584 --> 00:39:52,013
There's Satan's Triangle,

1260
00:39:52,013 --> 00:39:55,930
Lucifer's Elbow, uh, oh,
there, Devil's Desert.

1261
00:39:59,784 --> 00:40:02,384
- Flying over teenage skin eruptions, sir.

1262
00:40:02,384 --> 00:40:03,301
- [Tom] Ew.

1263
00:40:04,303 --> 00:40:06,485
(Tom laughs)

1264
00:40:06,485 --> 00:40:08,363
- Huh?
- We're landing there?

1265
00:40:08,363 --> 00:40:10,889
- You got a problem with that?

1266
00:40:10,889 --> 00:40:13,729
(Tom sings along with music)

1267
00:40:13,729 --> 00:40:15,069
- [Tom] Nice effect, though.

1268
00:40:15,069 --> 00:40:16,350
- Hold on tight!

1269
00:40:16,350 --> 00:40:17,708
This is going to be a rough one.

1270
00:40:17,708 --> 00:40:20,230
- [Tom] We'd better learn to get along.

1271
00:40:20,230 --> 00:40:21,800
- In the pipe, five by five.

1272
00:40:21,800 --> 00:40:24,383
(Tom chuckles)

1273
00:40:26,628 --> 00:40:28,230
- Careful, careful!

1274
00:40:28,230 --> 00:40:29,830
These sands are treacherous!

1275
00:40:29,830 --> 00:40:31,489
- They're headed straight for the dock!

1276
00:40:31,489 --> 00:40:33,670
(grunting)

1277
00:40:33,670 --> 00:40:35,121
(slamming)

1278
00:40:35,121 --> 00:40:37,371
(rumbling)

1279
00:40:40,689 --> 00:40:41,990
- [Joel] You know, this film

1280
00:40:41,990 --> 00:40:43,198
looks like it's scrapin' the bottom.

1281
00:40:43,198 --> 00:40:46,622
- Yeah, yeah.
- Well, should I let her down?

1282
00:40:46,622 --> 00:40:47,990
- Ah, note to myself.

1283
00:40:47,990 --> 00:40:49,880
Put landing gear on this baby.

1284
00:40:49,880 --> 00:40:52,062
(rumbling)

1285
00:40:52,062 --> 00:40:53,062
- [Tom] Ahh.

1286
00:40:55,921 --> 00:40:58,338
Arrakis, Dune, desert planet.

1287
00:41:02,340 --> 00:41:05,090
- Damn, I just washed this thing.

1288
00:41:06,353 --> 00:41:07,262
- [Joel] Looks like one of my old

1289
00:41:07,262 --> 00:41:08,661
ski club overnights, you know?

1290
00:41:08,661 --> 00:41:09,884
- [Tom] Ooh, Alpine Valley.

1291
00:41:09,884 --> 00:41:11,421
- [Joel] Yup.

1292
00:41:11,421 --> 00:41:14,873
- A planet that evolved from carob?

1293
00:41:14,873 --> 00:41:16,702
I don't think so.

1294
00:41:16,702 --> 00:41:20,513
♪ In-A-Gadda-Da-Vida, baby ♪

1295
00:41:20,513 --> 00:41:22,182
(groaning)

1296
00:41:22,182 --> 00:41:25,382
(uncertain music)

1297
00:41:25,382 --> 00:41:26,513
- [Ken] Tammy.

1298
00:41:26,513 --> 00:41:27,346
Tammy!

1299
00:41:27,346 --> 00:41:29,092
- [Tom] Tell me true.

1300
00:41:29,092 --> 00:41:30,134
- A girl?

1301
00:41:30,134 --> 00:41:32,398
A Grimald warrior's supposed to be brave!

1302
00:41:32,398 --> 00:41:33,279
- Yes.

1303
00:41:33,279 --> 00:41:34,112
- Get up.

1304
00:41:37,709 --> 00:41:38,588
Sir!

1305
00:41:38,588 --> 00:41:39,588
(Tom mimics snoring)
(Joel babbles)

1306
00:41:39,588 --> 00:41:41,838
- [Joel] Football practice!

1307
00:41:44,060 --> 00:41:46,380
- [Tom] Uh, what, what,
who turned off the TV set?

1308
00:41:46,380 --> 00:41:47,838
- Bloody Marys all around.

1309
00:41:47,838 --> 00:41:49,903
- (grunts) Come on,
pull yourself together.

1310
00:41:49,903 --> 00:41:52,345
- [Tom] Are they telling him
to pull yourself together?

1311
00:41:52,345 --> 00:41:54,224
- Ken, better check the others.

1312
00:41:54,224 --> 00:41:55,057
- Okay.

1313
00:41:55,057 --> 00:41:58,217
- Oh, yeah, aye-aye, captain.

1314
00:41:58,217 --> 00:42:00,050
- Dan! Snap out of it!

1315
00:42:00,926 --> 00:42:01,759
(Tom mimics snoring)

1316
00:42:01,759 --> 00:42:03,227
- Billy!
- Don't be a hero!

1317
00:42:03,227 --> 00:42:04,838
- [Ken] Colonel Yurulin!

1318
00:42:04,838 --> 00:42:06,715
- Ah, drive through clowns!

1319
00:42:06,715 --> 00:42:08,875
I want Sunrise Biscuit, come outta there!

1320
00:42:08,875 --> 00:42:10,595
- [Joe] Ah, will you look at that?

1321
00:42:10,595 --> 00:42:12,654
So hot in here it feels like a steam bath.

1322
00:42:12,654 --> 00:42:14,006
- [Joel] And me without a towel.

1323
00:42:14,006 --> 00:42:15,854
- Rocky, better get
the area on the screen.

1324
00:42:15,854 --> 00:42:16,687
- Okay.

1325
00:42:18,115 --> 00:42:19,886
- [Tom] Oh wow, they gotta
watch their own reruns?

1326
00:42:19,886 --> 00:42:21,022
What a nightmare.

1327
00:42:21,022 --> 00:42:23,060
- [Rocky] I wonder how
much damage we've got.

1328
00:42:23,060 --> 00:42:24,294
- I don't know.

1329
00:42:24,294 --> 00:42:26,563
I want every inch of
this craft checked out.

1330
00:42:26,563 --> 00:42:27,396
- Every inch.
- Yes, sir!

1331
00:42:27,396 --> 00:42:28,584
- Even the inch under your seat?

1332
00:42:28,584 --> 00:42:30,030
- Every inch, get to it.
- Every inch?

1333
00:42:30,030 --> 00:42:31,003
- Even the dirtiest inch in the kitchen?

1334
00:42:31,003 --> 00:42:32,165
- [Tom] Every single inch.

1335
00:42:32,165 --> 00:42:32,998
- [Crow] Even that inch that's--

1336
00:42:32,998 --> 00:42:33,831
- At least we're on the ground again.

1337
00:42:33,831 --> 00:42:35,476
- [Joel] Seems like there's
an inch over there that they--

1338
00:42:35,476 --> 00:42:37,257
- All right, I better go help the others.

1339
00:42:37,257 --> 00:42:40,340
(upbeat theme music)

1340
00:42:43,847 --> 00:42:45,967
- New from the Star Force
line of action figures,

1341
00:42:45,967 --> 00:42:47,916
it's Captain Joe, the boozy, brawling,

1342
00:42:47,916 --> 00:42:49,356
bloated Bacchus 3 commander

1343
00:42:49,356 --> 00:42:51,497
from the beloved Fugitive Alien series!

1344
00:42:51,497 --> 00:42:52,927
- Dizzy Gillespie cheeks sold separately.

1345
00:42:52,927 --> 00:42:55,785
- Yes, he swaggers, he
staggers, and he even talks.

1346
00:42:55,785 --> 00:42:58,023
- Uh, a fellow would do a lot worse

1347
00:42:58,023 --> 00:42:59,807
than touring with the lot of Bacchus 3.

1348
00:42:59,807 --> 00:43:01,097
Set 'em up, barkeep.

1349
00:43:01,097 --> 00:43:02,377
- Flask and travel bar not included.

1350
00:43:02,377 --> 00:43:04,047
- Yes, with your Captain Joe action figure

1351
00:43:04,047 --> 00:43:05,937
you'll be in a constant
state of excitement

1352
00:43:05,937 --> 00:43:07,527
while he's in a state of denial.

1353
00:43:07,527 --> 00:43:10,617
- Uh, I only drink on the weekend.

1354
00:43:10,617 --> 00:43:11,796
I can drink!

1355
00:43:11,796 --> 00:43:13,223
- Existential void where prohibited.

1356
00:43:13,223 --> 00:43:14,287
- Sure, he's got a problem,

1357
00:43:14,287 --> 00:43:15,708
but you don't have to
watch him deteriorate.

1358
00:43:15,708 --> 00:43:18,097
After all, you spent 9.95 for him!

1359
00:43:18,097 --> 00:43:19,206
- Tax and license not included!

1360
00:43:19,206 --> 00:43:20,798
- You can have hours
of fun as you organize

1361
00:43:20,798 --> 00:43:23,246
a crisis intervention for Captain Joe.

1362
00:43:23,246 --> 00:43:26,588
- [Joel] Captain Joe,
I am not gonna sit here

1363
00:43:26,588 --> 00:43:28,817
and watch you deteriorate.

1364
00:43:28,817 --> 00:43:32,798
Captain Joe, when Ken and
I had you over to eat,

1365
00:43:32,798 --> 00:43:35,249
you got drunk on cooking sherry,

1366
00:43:35,249 --> 00:43:36,988
and made a pass at me,

1367
00:43:36,988 --> 00:43:40,729
and threw up all over
the Malibu Dream House.

1368
00:43:40,729 --> 00:43:44,089
Captain Joe, dude, I loved you,

1369
00:43:44,089 --> 00:43:45,529
but I'm not gonna sit here

1370
00:43:45,529 --> 00:43:48,569
and watch you cowa-bungle your life.

1371
00:43:48,569 --> 00:43:49,969
- And don't forget, kids,

1372
00:43:49,969 --> 00:43:51,287
if Captain Joe refuses to deal

1373
00:43:51,287 --> 00:43:52,727
with the issues, you can always--

1374
00:43:52,727 --> 00:43:55,750
♪ Try to kill him with a forklift ♪

1375
00:43:55,750 --> 00:43:57,041
- 12 step workbook optional!

1376
00:43:57,041 --> 00:43:58,369
Product not included in some boxes.

1377
00:43:58,369 --> 00:44:00,201
Joe Namath netted slingshot
briefs sold separately.

1378
00:44:00,201 --> 00:44:01,881
(alarm buzzing)
- We got movie sign!

1379
00:44:01,881 --> 00:44:04,131
(shouting)

1380
00:44:11,332 --> 00:44:13,390
(dramatic, urgent music)

1381
00:44:13,390 --> 00:44:14,742
- Well, let's go.
(whistling)

1382
00:44:14,742 --> 00:44:15,852
- [Tom] Hey!

1383
00:44:15,852 --> 00:44:16,685
- Hey, where you goin'?

1384
00:44:16,685 --> 00:44:17,518
- [Joel] I'm sorry.

1385
00:44:17,518 --> 00:44:18,351
- [Tom] Thanks.

1386
00:44:18,351 --> 00:44:19,960
- You and Tammy are staying here.

1387
00:44:19,960 --> 00:44:21,060
- What for?

1388
00:44:21,060 --> 00:44:21,893
- As soon as we've left,

1389
00:44:21,893 --> 00:44:25,009
I want you bring Bacchus
3 to a safer place.

1390
00:44:25,009 --> 00:44:27,688
- Sir, do you think you're
doing the right thing?

1391
00:44:27,688 --> 00:44:28,540
- What do you mean?

1392
00:44:28,540 --> 00:44:32,260
- I was told when the
mission is dangerous, uh,

1393
00:44:32,260 --> 00:44:34,820
it's the older men who are
the ones to stay behind.

1394
00:44:34,820 --> 00:44:37,270
- [Joe] Rocky, that's an order.

1395
00:44:37,270 --> 00:44:38,590
- [Joel] Impressive eye contact.

1396
00:44:38,590 --> 00:44:39,809
- Sir, that's crazy!

1397
00:44:39,809 --> 00:44:41,246
You can't go on a forced march

1398
00:44:41,246 --> 00:44:42,486
through this desert at your age.

1399
00:44:42,486 --> 00:44:43,598
Let me go!

1400
00:44:43,598 --> 00:44:45,724
- I'll command my own mission.

1401
00:44:45,724 --> 00:44:46,557
- You--
- Pull my finger.

1402
00:44:46,557 --> 00:44:47,632
- Do as you're told.

1403
00:44:47,632 --> 00:44:48,936
I'll never shirk my responsibilities.

1404
00:44:48,936 --> 00:44:50,266
- Not even when my hip cracks.

1405
00:44:50,266 --> 00:44:52,185
(grave music)

1406
00:44:52,185 --> 00:44:55,155
- [Tom] Say.
(gun cocks)

1407
00:44:55,155 --> 00:44:56,488
- Rocky!
- Again?

1408
00:44:57,505 --> 00:44:59,715
- This is one order I can't obey.

1409
00:44:59,715 --> 00:45:01,654
- Disobey it over my dead body.

1410
00:45:01,654 --> 00:45:04,403
- Okay.
- Rocky, don't!

1411
00:45:04,403 --> 00:45:06,905
- Shoot me if you've got the guts.

1412
00:45:06,905 --> 00:45:08,814
My orders still stand!

1413
00:45:08,814 --> 00:45:10,265
- [Tom] Squeeze.
(gun fires)

1414
00:45:10,265 --> 00:45:11,283
(gasping)
- Hey.

1415
00:45:11,283 --> 00:45:12,994
(groaning)
He did it.

1416
00:45:12,994 --> 00:45:13,985
- [Tammy] Captain!

1417
00:45:13,985 --> 00:45:15,145
- [Tom] Oh, Captain, my captain!

1418
00:45:15,145 --> 00:45:16,646
- (grunts) I'll kill you for that!

1419
00:45:16,646 --> 00:45:17,885
- Don't get excited.

1420
00:45:17,885 --> 00:45:20,614
I wouldn't shoot my chief
with live ammunition.

1421
00:45:20,614 --> 00:45:21,774
It's a knockout dart.

1422
00:45:21,774 --> 00:45:22,775
- Of course, it pierced his colon.

1423
00:45:22,775 --> 00:45:25,843
- It'll just put him out of
commission for an hour or so.

1424
00:45:25,843 --> 00:45:27,714
Help me get him to some place comfortable.

1425
00:45:27,714 --> 00:45:29,185
Ken, grab his legs.

1426
00:45:29,185 --> 00:45:32,354
Now then, we've got a
mission to accomplish.

1427
00:45:32,354 --> 00:45:34,306
- [Tom] That is gonna be the
first time he's passed out cold

1428
00:45:34,306 --> 00:45:35,964
and he's gonna wake up sober! (chuckles)

1429
00:45:35,964 --> 00:45:36,935
- Peek-a-boo.

1430
00:45:36,935 --> 00:45:39,685
- [Joel] It's Abbott and
Costello in Turning Japanese.

1431
00:45:39,685 --> 00:45:41,727
(Tom sings riff from "Turning Japanese")

1432
00:45:41,727 --> 00:45:42,925
- All right, let's go.

1433
00:45:42,925 --> 00:45:45,643
(adventurous music)

1434
00:45:45,643 --> 00:45:47,916
- [Tom] And man was born of woman,

1435
00:45:47,916 --> 00:45:50,749
and they both inhabited the earth.

1436
00:45:51,786 --> 00:45:54,084
- Tammy, I want you to contact us

1437
00:45:54,084 --> 00:45:57,205
as soon as you've moved
Bacchus 3 to a safer place.

1438
00:45:57,205 --> 00:45:58,917
Call us on our micro-radios.
- Right.

1439
00:45:58,917 --> 00:46:01,037
- We'll try to maintain
contact from our end.

1440
00:46:01,037 --> 00:46:03,242
And don't forget, keep us in radar range.

1441
00:46:03,242 --> 00:46:05,218
- You can count one it.

1442
00:46:05,218 --> 00:46:07,167
- Oh, and, uh, you better
lock up the liquor cabinet

1443
00:46:07,167 --> 00:46:10,559
and hide the key, if you know what I mean.

1444
00:46:10,559 --> 00:46:14,298
♪ We're headed for adventure ♪

1445
00:46:14,298 --> 00:46:19,239
♪ We'll leave Tammy behind ♪

1446
00:46:19,239 --> 00:46:23,978
♪ We're gonna pad out the film some more ♪

1447
00:46:23,978 --> 00:46:27,718
♪ And you'll fall asleep ♪

1448
00:46:27,718 --> 00:46:28,919
♪ Three, four ♪

1449
00:46:28,919 --> 00:46:33,119
♪ We're climbing the sandy hill ♪

1450
00:46:33,119 --> 00:46:36,559
♪ Like you really care ♪
- That's good.

1451
00:46:36,559 --> 00:46:37,847
- [Joel] That's plenty.

1452
00:46:37,847 --> 00:46:39,245
- [Tom] Sorry.

1453
00:46:39,245 --> 00:46:40,078
- Faster!

1454
00:46:40,078 --> 00:46:41,558
- [Crew] Yes, sir.

1455
00:46:41,558 --> 00:46:42,698
- There's spiders all over me!

1456
00:46:42,698 --> 00:46:47,029
Get 'em off me, get 'em off me! (sobs)

1457
00:46:47,029 --> 00:46:48,599
- [Joel] You know, it's
the funniest sensation.

1458
00:46:48,599 --> 00:46:50,050
The room's not spinning.

1459
00:46:50,050 --> 00:46:50,883
Hm.
- Hm.

1460
00:46:52,570 --> 00:46:54,489
- I'll kill that Rocky.
- Again?

1461
00:46:54,489 --> 00:46:55,628
(Tom chuckles)

1462
00:46:55,628 --> 00:46:56,602
- [Tom] Hit him.

1463
00:46:56,602 --> 00:46:59,889
- [Joel] I took the liberty of
changing your jumpsuit, sir.

1464
00:46:59,889 --> 00:47:01,239
- Are they in radar range?
(beeping)

1465
00:47:01,239 --> 00:47:02,450
- Yes, sir.

1466
00:47:02,450 --> 00:47:03,941
They're right here on the screen.

1467
00:47:03,941 --> 00:47:06,108
22 degrees east-northeast.

1468
00:47:07,050 --> 00:47:09,230
(clicks)
(beeping)

1469
00:47:09,230 --> 00:47:10,359
- [Joel] I'm not in right now,

1470
00:47:10,359 --> 00:47:12,959
but if you'd like to leave
a message with my shoulder--

1471
00:47:12,959 --> 00:47:14,959
- Rocky, read me?
- Again?

1472
00:47:14,959 --> 00:47:15,792
(Tom chuckles)
- [Joel] Stop it.

1473
00:47:15,792 --> 00:47:17,343
- Rocky!
- Again?

1474
00:47:17,343 --> 00:47:18,176
- [Joel] Stop it!

1475
00:47:18,176 --> 00:47:19,352
- We're advancing on our objective.

1476
00:47:19,352 --> 00:47:22,134
- That was a dirty trick
you played on me. (grunts)

1477
00:47:22,134 --> 00:47:23,123
- [Rocky] Why don't you court martial me

1478
00:47:23,123 --> 00:47:25,352
over a cold beer when
this mission is over?

1479
00:47:25,352 --> 00:47:26,185
- [Tom] And a shot?

1480
00:47:26,185 --> 00:47:27,174
- All right.

1481
00:47:27,174 --> 00:47:28,904
I want you guys to be careful.

1482
00:47:28,904 --> 00:47:30,874
This is a very tricky operation.

1483
00:47:30,874 --> 00:47:34,214
- Yes, sir, and you get a good rest.

1484
00:47:34,214 --> 00:47:36,233
One of these days you'll
thank me for what I did.

1485
00:47:36,233 --> 00:47:38,355
- [Joel] Shoulder phone off.

1486
00:47:38,355 --> 00:47:39,688
- Rocky.
- Again?

1487
00:47:40,624 --> 00:47:41,555
- Sorry.

1488
00:47:41,555 --> 00:47:44,034
(radar beeping)
(determined music)

1489
00:47:44,034 --> 00:47:44,894
- [Tom] Pong?

1490
00:47:44,894 --> 00:47:45,727
Hmm.

1491
00:47:47,424 --> 00:47:49,075
- That Rocky.
- Again?

1492
00:47:49,075 --> 00:47:50,332
- I'll bust him when this is over.

1493
00:47:50,332 --> 00:47:51,652
(Joel grunts)

1494
00:47:51,652 --> 00:47:53,109
(Tammy giggles)

1495
00:47:53,109 --> 00:47:55,392
- [Joel] Sorry, I was thinking
about something else, sir.

1496
00:47:55,392 --> 00:47:58,021
(Tom sings along with score)

1497
00:47:58,021 --> 00:48:00,779
♪ We are marching on a big sand hill ♪

1498
00:48:00,779 --> 00:48:03,493
♪ We realize you've had your fill ♪

1499
00:48:03,493 --> 00:48:05,221
♪ As we march upon this big sand hill ♪

1500
00:48:05,221 --> 00:48:06,501
- [Joel] Just stop it.

1501
00:48:06,501 --> 00:48:07,334
- Hey, corn.

1502
00:48:07,334 --> 00:48:08,167
Hey, corn?

1503
00:48:08,167 --> 00:48:09,084
- Get down!

1504
00:48:11,090 --> 00:48:12,303
There's a watchtower.

1505
00:48:12,303 --> 00:48:13,999
- [Tom] Oh, but I kid
gentleman's witnesses,

1506
00:48:13,999 --> 00:48:15,140
ladies and gentlemen. (chuckles)

1507
00:48:15,140 --> 00:48:16,631
I love them.
(Crow chuckles)

1508
00:48:16,631 --> 00:48:18,283
(snare drumming)

1509
00:48:18,283 --> 00:48:20,249
- [Joel] Hey, check it out,
they're fighting ZZ Top!

1510
00:48:20,249 --> 00:48:21,587
- Oh.

1511
00:48:21,587 --> 00:48:22,597
(dramatic sting music)

1512
00:48:22,597 --> 00:48:23,507
- [Tom] Huh?

1513
00:48:23,507 --> 00:48:24,507
- Hey, Dave.

1514
00:48:26,518 --> 00:48:27,768
Oh, hiya, Evan.

1515
00:48:31,147 --> 00:48:32,226
- [Tom] I think they swiped this music

1516
00:48:32,226 --> 00:48:34,226
from Mission Impossible.

1517
00:48:38,249 --> 00:48:40,379
(Tom sings along with score)
- Get in as close as you can.

1518
00:48:40,379 --> 00:48:41,899
I'll try to divert the guards.

1519
00:48:41,899 --> 00:48:43,358
- And watch out for the percussionists.

1520
00:48:43,358 --> 00:48:46,038
They might have tambourines.

1521
00:48:46,038 --> 00:48:46,871
- [Tom] Let go of my leg.

1522
00:48:46,871 --> 00:48:48,707
- What's the matter, don't you trust me?

1523
00:48:48,707 --> 00:48:50,769
- What guarantee do we have
that you won't double cross us?

1524
00:48:50,769 --> 00:48:52,009
- [Joel] Oh, I'll leave you my keys.

1525
00:48:52,009 --> 00:48:54,435
- Look, if you attack that post head on,

1526
00:48:54,435 --> 00:48:55,809
those machine guns'll mow you down

1527
00:48:55,809 --> 00:48:57,009
in a matter of seconds.

1528
00:48:57,009 --> 00:48:57,926
- Hey, Moe!

1529
00:48:59,998 --> 00:49:01,516
- You know the way I feel.

1530
00:49:01,516 --> 00:49:03,339
I've got a score to
settle with this country.

1531
00:49:03,339 --> 00:49:06,489
- [Tom] And a song in my heart.

1532
00:49:06,489 --> 00:49:08,299
- [Joel] He's true to his school.

1533
00:49:08,299 --> 00:49:10,478
- Okay, I'll still keep you covered.

1534
00:49:10,478 --> 00:49:12,267
- Shh! Now.
- Shh.

1535
00:49:12,267 --> 00:49:16,017
(dramatic, foreboding music)

1536
00:49:18,358 --> 00:49:19,502
- Walk the way I walk.

1537
00:49:19,502 --> 00:49:22,169
All hunkered down like that.

1538
00:49:22,169 --> 00:49:23,587
- [Joel] Plan B, Merce Cunningham!

1539
00:49:23,587 --> 00:49:26,837
(subtle, sneaky music)

1540
00:49:32,939 --> 00:49:35,699
(Tom speaks in foreign language)

1541
00:49:35,699 --> 00:49:37,787
- [Joel] Hey, it's high definition TV.

1542
00:49:37,787 --> 00:49:38,870
- [Tom] Neat.

1543
00:49:43,106 --> 00:49:44,499
(Crow speaks in foreign language)

1544
00:49:44,499 --> 00:49:46,539
Oh, hey, you got a little
toilet paper on your shoe there.

1545
00:49:46,539 --> 00:49:47,372
(chuckles)

1546
00:49:47,372 --> 00:49:48,907
He's comin' out of the loo.

1547
00:49:48,907 --> 00:49:50,102
- Hi-keeba.

1548
00:49:50,102 --> 00:49:51,602
Now, on with the--

1549
00:49:53,449 --> 00:49:55,217
(Tom mutters)

1550
00:49:55,217 --> 00:49:57,740
- [Rocky] He did sell us out!

1551
00:49:57,740 --> 00:49:59,518
(alarm blares)

1552
00:49:59,518 --> 00:50:03,169
- [Joel] Uh, sir, it's
the Peter Frampton alarm!

1553
00:50:03,169 --> 00:50:04,835
Only goes off in the 70s.
- I should have known it.

1554
00:50:04,835 --> 00:50:07,136
- [Ken] A rat always returns to his hole.

1555
00:50:07,136 --> 00:50:10,134
(menacing music)
(alarm blares)

1556
00:50:10,134 --> 00:50:13,051
(Tom mimics alarm)

1557
00:50:14,931 --> 00:50:19,452
- [Tom] This is Operation
Desert Bore. (chuckles)

1558
00:50:19,452 --> 00:50:20,533
- [Joel] Sounds like the teacher

1559
00:50:20,533 --> 00:50:22,950
from the Peanuts TV specials.

1560
00:50:26,212 --> 00:50:27,914
(gun cocks)

1561
00:50:27,914 --> 00:50:29,344
- He's going to shoot us himself!

1562
00:50:29,344 --> 00:50:30,512
- Well, I'm flattered!
- Attack!

1563
00:50:30,512 --> 00:50:32,114
(shouting)

1564
00:50:32,114 --> 00:50:33,013
(machine gun fires)

1565
00:50:33,013 --> 00:50:35,034
- [Joel] Oh, no!

1566
00:50:35,034 --> 00:50:37,104
(screaming)

1567
00:50:37,104 --> 00:50:38,040
- Gallipoli.

1568
00:50:38,040 --> 00:50:39,501
- [Tom] Oh, neat.

1569
00:50:39,501 --> 00:50:40,708
(machine gun fires)
(screaming)

1570
00:50:40,708 --> 00:50:42,651
- [Joel] Cross of Iron, in color.

1571
00:50:42,651 --> 00:50:43,651
- [Tom] Ohh.

1572
00:50:45,091 --> 00:50:46,269
George!

1573
00:50:46,269 --> 00:50:47,141
Paul!

1574
00:50:47,141 --> 00:50:47,989
John!

1575
00:50:47,989 --> 00:50:48,822
Pete Best!

1576
00:50:49,851 --> 00:50:50,701
- You like my fort?

1577
00:50:50,701 --> 00:50:51,981
Made it out of refrigerator boxes!

1578
00:50:51,981 --> 00:50:53,749
- Come on out!
- Hooray!

1579
00:50:53,749 --> 00:50:55,598
- [Joel] Now it looks
like Lawrence of Arabia

1580
00:50:55,598 --> 00:50:58,119
except for the pink, shiny pleather suits.

1581
00:50:58,119 --> 00:50:59,178
(Tom chuckles)

1582
00:50:59,178 --> 00:51:01,880
(upbeat music)

1583
00:51:01,880 --> 00:51:02,869
- Ah, come on, girls!

1584
00:51:02,869 --> 00:51:04,020
(laughing)

1585
00:51:04,020 --> 00:51:05,861
- [Tom] (chuckles)
We're filled with mirth!

1586
00:51:05,861 --> 00:51:07,109
Mirth Cunningham!

1587
00:51:07,109 --> 00:51:09,691
- [Joel] Hey, where have
all the dead guys gone?

1588
00:51:09,691 --> 00:51:11,080
- [Tom] Aww.

1589
00:51:11,080 --> 00:51:13,899
- [Yurulin] Looks like I
had you worried for a while.

1590
00:51:13,899 --> 00:51:15,299
- You think anything's wrong?

1591
00:51:15,299 --> 00:51:17,050
- It seems all right so far, sir.

1592
00:51:17,050 --> 00:51:17,883
- Good.

1593
00:51:17,883 --> 00:51:18,931
- Hey, that Westinghouse symbol

1594
00:51:18,931 --> 00:51:20,627
kinda got wrecked in the crash.

1595
00:51:20,627 --> 00:51:21,491
(Tom chuckles)
- Tammy?

1596
00:51:21,491 --> 00:51:22,371
- [Tammy] Yes, sir.

1597
00:51:22,371 --> 00:51:23,540
- We've gotta get this ship out of here

1598
00:51:23,540 --> 00:51:25,411
before the next sandstorm.

1599
00:51:25,411 --> 00:51:26,531
That clear?

1600
00:51:26,531 --> 00:51:28,301
- (chuckles) Yes, sir.

1601
00:51:28,301 --> 00:51:30,109
- [Joel] Okay, now
here's the liquor store,

1602
00:51:30,109 --> 00:51:30,942
and there's Tom Thumb.

1603
00:51:30,942 --> 00:51:32,571
Now you take two lefts, and you're there.

1604
00:51:32,571 --> 00:51:33,404
No problem.
- This is it.

1605
00:51:33,404 --> 00:51:35,459
- [Yurulin] The red
star is a security zone.

1606
00:51:35,459 --> 00:51:37,179
- [Tom] (mimics radio
static) We are still 35 miles

1607
00:51:37,179 --> 00:51:38,680
to weather ship Tango Delta.

1608
00:51:38,680 --> 00:51:41,882
(triumphant music)

1609
00:51:41,882 --> 00:51:43,112
- Okay, now it's our turn to move.

1610
00:51:43,112 --> 00:51:44,352
Let's go!

1611
00:51:44,352 --> 00:51:46,019
- Hi-keeba, Captain.

1612
00:51:47,381 --> 00:51:49,272
(Tom sings along with score)

1613
00:51:49,272 --> 00:51:50,659
♪ Now strap in tight ♪

1614
00:51:50,659 --> 00:51:52,923
♪ Let's get set for action ♪

1615
00:51:52,923 --> 00:51:56,973
♪ To launch the ship out of the sand ♪

1616
00:51:56,973 --> 00:52:00,573
♪ He tried to kill us with a forklift ♪

1617
00:52:00,573 --> 00:52:02,292
- Huzzah! (chuckles)

1618
00:52:02,292 --> 00:52:03,292
I love that.

1619
00:52:07,992 --> 00:52:09,813
- [Narrator] While Captain
Joe moves the spacecraft

1620
00:52:09,813 --> 00:52:12,100
closer to the secret installation,

1621
00:52:12,100 --> 00:52:15,841
the crew of Bacchus 3,
disguised as Saysar soldiers,

1622
00:52:15,841 --> 00:52:17,508
advances cautiously.

1623
00:52:18,642 --> 00:52:20,340
- [Joel] Me? I'm Carl, the narrator.

1624
00:52:20,340 --> 00:52:21,991
I used to work with Ken.

1625
00:52:21,991 --> 00:52:25,247
I do these voiceovers to finance
what I really want to do.

1626
00:52:25,247 --> 00:52:26,290
- [Tom] And what's that, Carl?

1627
00:52:26,290 --> 00:52:27,123
- [Joel] Decoupage.

1628
00:52:27,123 --> 00:52:28,531
- [Tom] (laughs) Thank you.

1629
00:52:28,531 --> 00:52:30,340
- What are they doing at the
Joshua Tree National Forest?

1630
00:52:30,340 --> 00:52:31,831
- [Tom] You got me.

1631
00:52:31,831 --> 00:52:33,998
(beeping)

1632
00:52:36,610 --> 00:52:38,171
- [Joel] Oh, now this is the nice side

1633
00:52:38,171 --> 00:52:39,498
of the Devil's Desert.

1634
00:52:39,498 --> 00:52:41,331
- [Tom] Oh, of course.

1635
00:52:42,732 --> 00:52:43,778
- [Rocky] Have they got the super weapon

1636
00:52:43,778 --> 00:52:45,039
stored in this depot?

1637
00:52:45,039 --> 00:52:46,479
- No, but they've got Mr. Freezies.

1638
00:52:46,479 --> 00:52:48,039
- [Yurulin] It must be here.

1639
00:52:48,039 --> 00:52:48,872
- [Ken] It sure doesn't look

1640
00:52:48,872 --> 00:52:51,019
like a high security installation.

1641
00:52:51,019 --> 00:52:52,960
- Yeah, looks like nothing.
- Yeah.

1642
00:52:52,960 --> 00:52:54,079
- Guess most of it's underground.

1643
00:52:54,079 --> 00:52:55,848
- [Tom] Yeah, they even got a
bowling alley in the basement.

1644
00:52:55,848 --> 00:52:59,931
It's just like the White
House, it's really cool.

1645
00:53:01,309 --> 00:53:02,488
- [Joel] It's a nature outing.

1646
00:53:02,488 --> 00:53:04,077
- [Tom] Oh, how charming.

1647
00:53:04,077 --> 00:53:05,219
- Stop here.

1648
00:53:05,219 --> 00:53:07,408
- Wait, there's your punch!

1649
00:53:07,408 --> 00:53:08,909
- [Joel] Damn, zither balls everywhere!

1650
00:53:08,909 --> 00:53:09,742
- Oh, no!

1651
00:53:10,808 --> 00:53:11,810
- [Tom] Okay.

1652
00:53:11,810 --> 00:53:12,643
Ahh.

1653
00:53:12,643 --> 00:53:14,629
- [Yurulin] Don't go near that!

1654
00:53:14,629 --> 00:53:18,456
- [Tom] Looks like we're
in the Giraffe Lot here.

1655
00:53:18,456 --> 00:53:19,289
Hm?

1656
00:53:20,600 --> 00:53:22,720
- [Joel] Hm, he's makin' somethin'.

1657
00:53:22,720 --> 00:53:23,960
(grunting)

1658
00:53:23,960 --> 00:53:24,829
(electricity crackles)
- [Tom] Ooh!

1659
00:53:24,829 --> 00:53:26,162
- Oh.
- Hi-keeba.

1660
00:53:28,272 --> 00:53:29,611
- Well.

1661
00:53:29,611 --> 00:53:31,880
Good thing we're not branches.

1662
00:53:31,880 --> 00:53:33,581
- It's just as I thought.

1663
00:53:33,581 --> 00:53:34,520
They've got the whole installation

1664
00:53:34,520 --> 00:53:36,051
surrounded by a lethal ray.

1665
00:53:36,051 --> 00:53:37,621
- Martha Raye.
- Wow.

1666
00:53:37,621 --> 00:53:39,451
- That's all we need.

1667
00:53:39,451 --> 00:53:43,181
- This super weapon must be
an incredibly powerful device

1668
00:53:43,181 --> 00:53:47,551
if they need this elaborate
a system to protect it.

1669
00:53:47,551 --> 00:53:49,151
- No, Ken, don't try it.

1670
00:53:49,151 --> 00:53:51,398
- [Joel] Yeah, nice canky
you're workin' on there, Rocky.

1671
00:53:51,398 --> 00:53:53,328
- [Yurulin] It'll vaporize you in seconds.

1672
00:53:53,328 --> 00:53:57,120
(grunting)
(Joel and bots grunt)

1673
00:53:57,120 --> 00:53:58,848
- Huh?
- How?

1674
00:53:58,848 --> 00:54:00,376
- The Fosbury flop!

1675
00:54:00,376 --> 00:54:02,006
- [Joel] They've discovered Flubber!

1676
00:54:02,006 --> 00:54:03,037
Hoo hoo!

1677
00:54:03,037 --> 00:54:04,499
What fun! (chuckles)

1678
00:54:04,499 --> 00:54:06,155
- [Tom] Woo-hoo-hoo-hoo.

1679
00:54:06,155 --> 00:54:08,027
- [Ken] Okay, Billy,
you're next. Let's go.

1680
00:54:08,027 --> 00:54:09,046
- What about my rifle?

1681
00:54:09,046 --> 00:54:09,879
- Watch!
- There you are!

1682
00:54:09,879 --> 00:54:10,712
- There's your rifle!

1683
00:54:10,712 --> 00:54:13,962
(Joel and bots babble)

1684
00:54:15,118 --> 00:54:17,109
- That red spot hasn't moved an inch.

1685
00:54:17,109 --> 00:54:19,156
- But it's healing nicely.
- I hope they're all right.

1686
00:54:19,156 --> 00:54:21,766
- (chuckles) They'll be fine.

1687
00:54:21,766 --> 00:54:23,316
They know if they blow this one,

1688
00:54:23,316 --> 00:54:26,408
I'm gonna kick them
right out of the service.

1689
00:54:26,408 --> 00:54:28,230
- You remind me of my father.

1690
00:54:28,230 --> 00:54:30,597
- [Joel] Oh, let's keep
our mind on our (coughs)

1691
00:54:30,597 --> 00:54:32,078
work, shall we?

1692
00:54:32,078 --> 00:54:33,507
Hoo hoo, it's fun!

1693
00:54:33,507 --> 00:54:36,267
You're my friend!
(Tom babbles)

1694
00:54:36,267 --> 00:54:38,259
- [Rocky] Having a Star Wolf
along has its advantages.

1695
00:54:38,259 --> 00:54:40,138
- Rocky, let's go.
- I'm with you.

1696
00:54:40,138 --> 00:54:44,378
- [Tom] And without you. (chuckles)

1697
00:54:44,378 --> 00:54:46,769
♪ Sandy Frank ♪

1698
00:54:46,769 --> 00:54:47,630
(Tom sings)

1699
00:54:47,630 --> 00:54:49,790
Oh, wait, musical.

1700
00:54:49,790 --> 00:54:51,950
- [Joel] All boring on the western front.

1701
00:54:51,950 --> 00:54:52,889
(Tom chuckles)

1702
00:54:52,889 --> 00:54:54,748
- I'll say.
- Rocky?

1703
00:54:54,748 --> 00:54:55,708
- Come over here.

1704
00:54:55,708 --> 00:54:56,541
- Again?

1705
00:54:56,541 --> 00:54:57,497
- [Tom] Oh, he did it again.

1706
00:54:57,497 --> 00:54:58,598
- I'm way over here.

1707
00:54:58,598 --> 00:55:01,049
- Look, check that out
with your field classes.

1708
00:55:01,049 --> 00:55:04,799
(babbling and cross-talking)

1709
00:55:07,195 --> 00:55:09,278
- Hm.
- Say, not half bad!

1710
00:55:10,347 --> 00:55:12,627
- So it is underground.

1711
00:55:12,627 --> 00:55:13,460
- Rocky!

1712
00:55:13,460 --> 00:55:15,967
♪ There's a world going on ♪

1713
00:55:15,967 --> 00:55:17,057
♪ Underground ♪

1714
00:55:17,057 --> 00:55:18,187
(Tom sings)

1715
00:55:18,187 --> 00:55:19,020
- It's us!

1716
00:55:19,020 --> 00:55:23,437
Hey, wait a minute, did we
just do another hop thing?

1717
00:55:25,177 --> 00:55:26,830
- [Joel] Hey, it's us again.

1718
00:55:26,830 --> 00:55:29,921
Are we unstuck in time or something?

1719
00:55:29,921 --> 00:55:32,087
- [Rocky] It won't be easy
getting into this place.

1720
00:55:32,087 --> 00:55:33,699
- How will we do it?

1721
00:55:33,699 --> 00:55:35,022
- Easy.
- Wait a minute.

1722
00:55:35,022 --> 00:55:36,668
- Those ID tags.

1723
00:55:36,668 --> 00:55:37,901
If we can get our hands on them,

1724
00:55:37,901 --> 00:55:39,230
we can waltz right through.

1725
00:55:39,230 --> 00:55:40,721
- Why not take the whole uniform?

1726
00:55:40,721 --> 00:55:42,011
- [Tom] And rumba right in.

1727
00:55:42,011 --> 00:55:44,081
- I'm Chet, welcome to
Arby's training school.

1728
00:55:44,081 --> 00:55:46,441
Again, I'm Chet if you need anything.

1729
00:55:46,441 --> 00:55:47,274
I'll write it down.

1730
00:55:47,274 --> 00:55:48,561
(goofy music)

1731
00:55:48,561 --> 00:55:50,251
- [Joel] Are you seein' what I'm seein'?

1732
00:55:50,251 --> 00:55:51,302
They're nude!

1733
00:55:51,302 --> 00:55:52,668
- Oh-hoo!

1734
00:55:52,668 --> 00:55:54,401
- Good luck.

1735
00:55:54,401 --> 00:55:56,251
- [Tom] Artie Johnson, I thought so!

1736
00:55:56,251 --> 00:55:59,580
(Crow sings along with score)

1737
00:55:59,580 --> 00:56:00,971
- Jack Sue.

1738
00:56:00,971 --> 00:56:01,971
- [Tom] Hey.

1739
00:56:02,972 --> 00:56:05,222
Boots are made for walkin'.

1740
00:56:08,250 --> 00:56:12,061
(Tom sings along with score)

1741
00:56:12,061 --> 00:56:13,621
♪ Lay down a boogie ♪

1742
00:56:13,621 --> 00:56:16,309
♪ And play that funky music till you die ♪

1743
00:56:16,309 --> 00:56:18,697
(struggling)

1744
00:56:18,697 --> 00:56:20,856
- Jack Oakie?
- Pass.

1745
00:56:20,856 --> 00:56:22,389
- [Tom] Huh?

1746
00:56:22,389 --> 00:56:24,056
- Oh, that was easy.

1747
00:56:26,429 --> 00:56:27,298
Again, I'm Chet.

1748
00:56:27,298 --> 00:56:28,809
- [Guard] Haven't seen
those guys here before.

1749
00:56:28,809 --> 00:56:30,017
- [Joel] Nice lookin' guys, though.

1750
00:56:30,017 --> 00:56:30,850
- You know how it is,

1751
00:56:30,850 --> 00:56:32,616
they're always sending in reinforcements.

1752
00:56:32,616 --> 00:56:36,330
- [Tom] We are 22 minutes
to weather ship Tango Delta.

1753
00:56:36,330 --> 00:56:37,497
- Captain!

1754
00:56:37,497 --> 00:56:38,600
- I saw it.

1755
00:56:38,600 --> 00:56:40,600
- They made it inside.

1756
00:56:40,600 --> 00:56:41,433
I knew they would.

1757
00:56:41,433 --> 00:56:42,350
- [Tom] Oh.

1758
00:56:45,838 --> 00:56:50,838
(hesitant music)
(Tom sings along)

1759
00:56:53,570 --> 00:56:54,403
Hmm.

1760
00:56:56,181 --> 00:56:58,141
- He got the coal mine, I got the shaft.

1761
00:56:58,141 --> 00:56:59,838
(Tom chuckles)

1762
00:56:59,838 --> 00:57:02,960
- [Joel] It's Bruce Lee, and Bruce Lee

1763
00:57:02,960 --> 00:57:05,120
in a collision course with wackiness!

1764
00:57:05,120 --> 00:57:08,000
(Tom chuckles)

1765
00:57:08,000 --> 00:57:10,088
- Crotch cam, I'm huge!

1766
00:57:10,088 --> 00:57:12,671
(Tom chuckles)

1767
00:57:14,368 --> 00:57:18,118
(Tom sings along with score)

1768
00:57:21,498 --> 00:57:23,368
- [Joel] Hey, do you
guys have a hall pass?

1769
00:57:23,368 --> 00:57:24,201
Come on.

1770
00:57:25,136 --> 00:57:26,509
- Hi-keeba, get that suit pressed.

1771
00:57:26,509 --> 00:57:28,138
And trim the hair in our nose.

1772
00:57:28,138 --> 00:57:29,738
That's all.

1773
00:57:29,738 --> 00:57:30,571
(sudden, dramatic music)

1774
00:57:30,571 --> 00:57:32,749
- [Tom] Zither lamps everywhere!

1775
00:57:32,749 --> 00:57:34,120
Huzzah.

1776
00:57:34,120 --> 00:57:36,287
(panting)

1777
00:57:38,127 --> 00:57:39,349
Nice boots.

1778
00:57:39,349 --> 00:57:41,800
- [Joel] Over here, a little
further, behind this rock.

1779
00:57:41,800 --> 00:57:42,883
Yeah, mm-hmm.

1780
00:57:43,760 --> 00:57:47,138
- For the walking sequence,
special director Roger Corman.

1781
00:57:47,138 --> 00:57:49,638
- [Tom] Quit panting, shut up!

1782
00:57:52,629 --> 00:57:53,759
(Crow whistles)
- [Joel] Nothing, nothing.

1783
00:57:53,759 --> 00:57:57,048
Act natural, hi!
(bots hum casually)

1784
00:57:57,048 --> 00:57:57,881
- Now!

1785
00:57:57,881 --> 00:57:59,528
- [Tom] Garrison's Gorillas, in color!

1786
00:57:59,528 --> 00:58:01,440
(hesitant music)

1787
00:58:01,440 --> 00:58:04,690
(Tom sings with score)

1788
00:58:06,848 --> 00:58:07,681
- [Soldiers] Saysar!

1789
00:58:07,681 --> 00:58:08,514
- Romero!

1790
00:58:08,514 --> 00:58:13,514
- [Tom] Did somebody say
Cesar Romero? (chuckles)

1791
00:58:13,979 --> 00:58:15,461
- Okay, let's do it now.

1792
00:58:15,461 --> 00:58:16,570
- [Tom] What, here?

1793
00:58:16,570 --> 00:58:17,992
Here?
- Right now.

1794
00:58:17,992 --> 00:58:18,825
- Hold it.

1795
00:58:21,353 --> 00:58:23,232
(Tom sings along with score)

1796
00:58:23,232 --> 00:58:24,065
Now!

1797
00:58:24,065 --> 00:58:26,315
(grunting)

1798
00:58:30,920 --> 00:58:33,463
- [Joel] It's mom's old Vaudeville stuff!

1799
00:58:33,463 --> 00:58:36,252
- [Tom] What do ya know?

1800
00:58:36,252 --> 00:58:40,761
Wait a minute, it's the
lobby at Caesar's Palace!

1801
00:58:40,761 --> 00:58:41,844
I thought so.

1802
00:58:43,873 --> 00:58:45,161
- Cool.

1803
00:58:45,161 --> 00:58:47,631
(menacing music)

1804
00:58:47,631 --> 00:58:50,041
- [Tom] Are they blue or not?

1805
00:58:50,041 --> 00:58:51,023
- [Joel] The plastic thing!

1806
00:58:51,023 --> 00:58:51,856
- [Tom] Ooh!

1807
00:58:51,856 --> 00:58:53,382
- I can smash this alone.

1808
00:58:53,382 --> 00:58:54,561
Is that all their is to it?

1809
00:58:54,561 --> 00:58:56,387
- Quiet! Just wait.

1810
00:58:56,387 --> 00:58:58,181
Your superhuman strength may not be enough

1811
00:58:58,181 --> 00:58:59,891
against a machine like that.

1812
00:58:59,891 --> 00:59:01,841
We've gotta do this slowly and carefully.

1813
00:59:01,841 --> 00:59:04,091
- So you can thoroughly bore the viewers.

1814
00:59:04,091 --> 00:59:06,022
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

1815
00:59:06,022 --> 00:59:07,189
- Whoa.
- Neat.

1816
00:59:08,607 --> 00:59:09,678
- [Tom] Guys, I'm having
a hard time telling

1817
00:59:09,678 --> 00:59:10,628
how big this things is.

1818
00:59:10,628 --> 00:59:11,578
Can we have something on the screen

1819
00:59:11,578 --> 00:59:13,538
to figure out the scale here?

1820
00:59:13,538 --> 00:59:14,978
- [Announcer] Attention, attention.

1821
00:59:14,978 --> 00:59:17,407
This is Field Marshall Telsa,
your commander-in-chief.

1822
00:59:17,407 --> 00:59:18,240
- And Grand Poobah!

1823
00:59:18,240 --> 00:59:20,239
- [Tesla] I am proud to
announce that a new age

1824
00:59:20,239 --> 00:59:21,690
has begun for the people of Saysar.

1825
00:59:21,690 --> 00:59:23,519
- [Joel] Oh, that explains the crystals.

1826
00:59:23,519 --> 00:59:24,972
- Ohh.

1827
00:59:24,972 --> 00:59:26,458
- [Tom] New age and all.

1828
00:59:26,458 --> 00:59:28,530
- [Tesla] We can meet any challenge.

1829
00:59:28,530 --> 00:59:31,338
Not even the supposedly
invincible Wolf Raiders

1830
00:59:31,338 --> 00:59:34,327
from Valna star can threaten us anymore.

1831
00:59:34,327 --> 00:59:35,548
From now on, we shall be able to--

1832
00:59:35,548 --> 00:59:37,098
- [Tom] Oh! Sorry, ladies.

1833
00:59:37,098 --> 00:59:39,175
- [Tesla] And destroy their very planet.

1834
00:59:39,175 --> 00:59:40,569
- [Tom] Lunch today is chicken-fried stake

1835
00:59:40,569 --> 00:59:41,988
and whipped potatoes.

1836
00:59:41,988 --> 00:59:43,818
- Are ready to dominate world!

1837
00:59:43,818 --> 00:59:45,828
Sir, we've achieved
the final breakthrough!

1838
00:59:45,828 --> 00:59:46,661
We're getting ready to--

1839
00:59:46,661 --> 00:59:47,818
- No speeches, solider!

1840
00:59:47,818 --> 00:59:49,679
Get back to your post.
- Please excuse me, sir.

1841
00:59:49,679 --> 00:59:51,559
- I promise to pay more
attention to my duties.

1842
00:59:51,559 --> 00:59:53,248
- [Joel] What a dope, hit him!

1843
00:59:53,248 --> 00:59:54,081
Come on.

1844
00:59:56,879 --> 00:59:59,050
- Halt! Nobody's allowed past this point.

1845
00:59:59,050 --> 01:00:00,399
- You must be a new recruit.

1846
01:00:00,399 --> 01:00:01,628
- No, sir, a blue recruit!

1847
01:00:01,628 --> 01:00:03,620
- Go on in.
- Yes, sir, right away.

1848
01:00:03,620 --> 01:00:05,037
- Out of the way.

1849
01:00:07,948 --> 01:00:08,958
- [New Recruit] Sir, I
was ordered not to let

1850
01:00:08,958 --> 01:00:10,750
anyone past this point.
- These men are all right.

1851
01:00:10,750 --> 01:00:12,835
- [Joel] They're really good
guys, especially that Chopper.

1852
01:00:12,835 --> 01:00:13,998
He's a nut.

1853
01:00:13,998 --> 01:00:16,165
- [Tom] All done in there?

1854
01:00:21,807 --> 01:00:23,278
- It's a Super Tom Servo

1855
01:00:23,278 --> 01:00:25,030
with thrush-busters and glass packs!

1856
01:00:25,030 --> 01:00:25,952
Wow!

1857
01:00:25,952 --> 01:00:28,198
- [Tom] Tunnel rim, four barrel!

1858
01:00:28,198 --> 01:00:29,628
- Chopped and channeled.

1859
01:00:29,628 --> 01:00:30,711
- [Tom] Cool.

1860
01:00:31,829 --> 01:00:32,956
- Look at that!

1861
01:00:32,956 --> 01:00:34,058
- Like a beating heart!

1862
01:00:34,058 --> 01:00:36,779
- [Tom] Like a beating heart
liberal! (chuckles and coughs)

1863
01:00:36,779 --> 01:00:38,128
- Ken, you plant the time bomb.

1864
01:00:38,128 --> 01:00:38,961
- Okay.

1865
01:00:40,556 --> 01:00:43,806
(subtle, sneaky music)

1866
01:00:45,566 --> 01:00:46,459
- Wait, they're gonna destroy it

1867
01:00:46,459 --> 01:00:48,478
with refrigerator magnets?

1868
01:00:48,478 --> 01:00:52,048
- Yes, my detachment was on maneuvers

1869
01:00:52,048 --> 01:00:54,040
in the northernmost part of the country.

1870
01:00:54,040 --> 01:00:57,030
- [Joel] Yeah, it was a
blast, it was really fun.

1871
01:00:57,030 --> 01:00:59,670
- [Tom] You're a sleek, young fellow.

1872
01:00:59,670 --> 01:01:01,699
Thin, trim.
- It's an honor to serve here.

1873
01:01:01,699 --> 01:01:03,419
- Yes, sir, I know that sir.

1874
01:01:03,419 --> 01:01:04,879
We had a competition in our unit.

1875
01:01:04,879 --> 01:01:06,160
- I was the bluest.
- I was the winner.

1876
01:01:06,160 --> 01:01:07,499
- That's why I was selected for guard duty

1877
01:01:07,499 --> 01:01:08,728
at this installation.

1878
01:01:08,728 --> 01:01:09,561
- [Joel] Ah, you've created

1879
01:01:09,561 --> 01:01:11,478
quite a little world for yourself, I see.

1880
01:01:11,478 --> 01:01:14,061
(Tom chuckles)

1881
01:01:16,291 --> 01:01:17,131
- Hide the bomb.

1882
01:01:17,131 --> 01:01:18,239
It's Yurulin with that kid.

1883
01:01:18,239 --> 01:01:19,182
- [Yurulin] Open the door!

1884
01:01:19,182 --> 01:01:20,600
I haven't got all day!

1885
01:01:20,600 --> 01:01:21,471
- [Tom] Well, I do,

1886
01:01:21,471 --> 01:01:24,552
but I don't wanna give it all
up for this is what I mean.

1887
01:01:24,552 --> 01:01:25,791
- Everything all right?

1888
01:01:25,791 --> 01:01:27,262
- [Ken] Yes sir, everything's just fine.

1889
01:01:27,262 --> 01:01:28,679
- Good, let's go.

1890
01:01:31,280 --> 01:01:33,591
- [Tom] Bye, thanks for the check up.

1891
01:01:33,591 --> 01:01:34,674
He's so cool.

1892
01:01:36,951 --> 01:01:39,451
(door closes)

1893
01:01:43,091 --> 01:01:43,971
Thanks.

1894
01:01:43,971 --> 01:01:45,851
- You're a fine soldier!

1895
01:01:45,851 --> 01:01:47,491
The next time I see your commander,

1896
01:01:47,491 --> 01:01:49,080
I'll tell him you're doing a good job.

1897
01:01:49,080 --> 01:01:50,400
- Oh, thank you, Colonel.

1898
01:01:50,400 --> 01:01:51,272
- Let's do lunch.

1899
01:01:51,272 --> 01:01:52,105
You're it.

1900
01:01:53,331 --> 01:01:54,164
- [Joel] I could talk to that guy

1901
01:01:54,164 --> 01:01:56,331
till I'm blue in the face.

1902
01:01:57,323 --> 01:01:59,573
(Tom hums)

1903
01:02:02,712 --> 01:02:04,211
- Thanks for keeping him distracted.

1904
01:02:04,211 --> 01:02:05,542
The time bombs are ready to go off.

1905
01:02:05,542 --> 01:02:07,809
- [Tom] Oh, he's a swell
kid, hate to see him die.

1906
01:02:07,809 --> 01:02:10,892
(upbeat theme music)

1907
01:02:15,683 --> 01:02:17,742
- They're playing my song!

1908
01:02:17,742 --> 01:02:19,728
(orchestrated music)

1909
01:02:19,728 --> 01:02:21,752
- [Tom] Kirk Listing number 15,

1910
01:02:21,752 --> 01:02:23,669
Eine kleine Nachtmusik.

1911
01:02:25,773 --> 01:02:27,511
- [Joel] Masterpiece
Theater is brought to you

1912
01:02:27,511 --> 01:02:30,678
by a grant from the Mobil Corporation.

1913
01:02:32,261 --> 01:02:34,130
- You can't just stand there, sir.

1914
01:02:34,130 --> 01:02:35,629
- Watch me.

1915
01:02:35,629 --> 01:02:37,829
- We've got to get out of here.

1916
01:02:37,829 --> 01:02:39,829
- This is our Saysar anthem.

1917
01:02:39,829 --> 01:02:41,461
- So what?

1918
01:02:41,461 --> 01:02:43,720
- Every day at this hour,
we all stand at attention

1919
01:02:43,720 --> 01:02:46,640
and renew our loyalty to the homeland.

1920
01:02:46,640 --> 01:02:47,473
- That's great.

1921
01:02:47,473 --> 01:02:50,209
While the others are standing
at attention, we'll get out.

1922
01:02:50,209 --> 01:02:51,529
- Yeah, that's great,
you stand at attention,

1923
01:02:51,529 --> 01:02:52,741
and I'll pick you up and carry ya.

1924
01:02:52,741 --> 01:02:53,574
Come on!

1925
01:02:53,574 --> 01:02:55,170
- [Joel] Hey, are those
Blaupunkt speakers?

1926
01:02:55,170 --> 01:02:57,109
They sound great.

1927
01:02:57,109 --> 01:02:59,821
♪ And the home of the brave ♪

1928
01:02:59,821 --> 01:03:01,000
(Tom hocks and spits)

1929
01:03:01,000 --> 01:03:02,629
- Hey, buddy.
- What's wrong?

1930
01:03:02,629 --> 01:03:03,796
- Can he hear?

1931
01:03:05,530 --> 01:03:07,078
Colonel!
- Psst!

1932
01:03:07,078 --> 01:03:10,072
- [Joel] Exnay on the edgeplay!

1933
01:03:10,072 --> 01:03:11,592
- It's that music.

1934
01:03:11,592 --> 01:03:12,832
It has an effect on him.

1935
01:03:12,832 --> 01:03:15,501
When he hears it, he snaps to attention.

1936
01:03:15,501 --> 01:03:17,001
- The guy's crazy!

1937
01:03:17,001 --> 01:03:19,381
We've got no time for patriotism now.

1938
01:03:19,381 --> 01:03:20,871
That bomb is about to go off.

1939
01:03:20,871 --> 01:03:22,370
Colonel, we gotta get out of here!

1940
01:03:22,370 --> 01:03:24,322
Come on down, sir,
there's no time to lose!

1941
01:03:24,322 --> 01:03:25,250
- [Tom] Huh?

1942
01:03:25,250 --> 01:03:26,722
- My country needs me!
- Colonel!

1943
01:03:26,722 --> 01:03:28,301
- You know, his country
would win more wars

1944
01:03:28,301 --> 01:03:30,539
if its national anthem was shorter.

1945
01:03:30,539 --> 01:03:31,449
- What happened to you?

1946
01:03:31,449 --> 01:03:34,709
- [Joel] Somebody finger-painted me!

1947
01:03:34,709 --> 01:03:35,792
- Spy attack.

1948
01:03:36,830 --> 01:03:39,089
- [Tom] Get off my chest.

1949
01:03:39,089 --> 01:03:40,668
- [Soldier] Red alert! Red alert!

1950
01:03:40,668 --> 01:03:42,801
- Message received, nobody gets in here.

1951
01:03:42,801 --> 01:03:45,139
- Without a tuxedo and
a note from Mr. Gotti!

1952
01:03:45,139 --> 01:03:45,972
- You can't go in there!

1953
01:03:45,972 --> 01:03:47,619
- Out of my way!

1954
01:03:47,619 --> 01:03:48,531
- [Tom] Infidel.

1955
01:03:48,531 --> 01:03:49,619
- Stay where you are!

1956
01:03:49,619 --> 01:03:51,361
One more step and I'll shoot!
(gun fires)

1957
01:03:51,361 --> 01:03:52,481
- [Joel] He didn't take a step.

1958
01:03:52,481 --> 01:03:55,441
What is he, a Chicago cop, that guy?

1959
01:03:55,441 --> 01:03:57,371
- [Tom] Oh look, he's doing Joe Cocker.

1960
01:03:57,371 --> 01:03:59,790
♪ What would you think ♪

1961
01:03:59,790 --> 01:04:01,491
- Harvey's lost one good worker.

1962
01:04:01,491 --> 01:04:03,521
He was the best damn fry cook they had.

1963
01:04:03,521 --> 01:04:04,641
(tuts)

1964
01:04:04,641 --> 01:04:06,171
- [Tom] Adios, sweet friend.

1965
01:04:06,171 --> 01:04:09,338
- [Joel] Space Camp with Kate Capshaw.

1966
01:04:11,851 --> 01:04:15,019
- [Tom] We are unable to
reach the primary target, sir.

1967
01:04:15,019 --> 01:04:18,041
We will go to alternate target at Laputa.

1968
01:04:18,041 --> 01:04:20,030
- It's 15 minutes.
- We're not famous anymore.

1969
01:04:20,030 --> 01:04:21,121
- Ken and the others aren't out.

1970
01:04:21,121 --> 01:04:23,553
There's something wrong, sir.

1971
01:04:23,553 --> 01:04:25,112
- I have confidence in them.

1972
01:04:25,112 --> 01:04:26,571
They're all professionals.

1973
01:04:26,571 --> 01:04:29,001
- [Joel] Yeah, I'll be inside
a bottle if you need me.

1974
01:04:29,001 --> 01:04:31,918
- [Tom] I hate patronizing answers.

1975
01:04:36,003 --> 01:04:37,942
(zapping)
(yelps)

1976
01:04:37,942 --> 01:04:39,462
- [Tom] Hm. Ooh.

1977
01:04:39,462 --> 01:04:40,323
(yelping)

1978
01:04:40,323 --> 01:04:42,166
- Our prisoners are baked, not fried.

1979
01:04:42,166 --> 01:04:43,886
- [Billy] Dan!

1980
01:04:43,886 --> 01:04:45,206
Dan!

1981
01:04:45,206 --> 01:04:46,039
- Billy!

1982
01:04:46,039 --> 01:04:47,765
- [Tom] Do not attempt to adjust your TV.

1983
01:04:47,765 --> 01:04:50,097
- Don't wait for me, go on ahead.

1984
01:04:50,097 --> 01:04:51,067
(gun fires)

1985
01:04:51,067 --> 01:04:54,006
- [Tom] Oh, wait, shootin' the wrong guy.

1986
01:04:54,006 --> 01:04:55,947
- Billy, save yourself!

1987
01:04:55,947 --> 01:04:56,780
- [Enemy] There they are!

1988
01:04:56,780 --> 01:04:59,987
- [Joel] Laser wall by Peter Max.

1989
01:04:59,987 --> 01:05:00,906
(guns fire)

1990
01:05:00,906 --> 01:05:02,124
(Tom sings along with score)

1991
01:05:02,124 --> 01:05:03,455
- [Dan] Billy, don't
try to fight them off!

1992
01:05:03,455 --> 01:05:04,676
Run for it!

1993
01:05:04,676 --> 01:05:06,156
- I'll come back for you, Dan!

1994
01:05:06,156 --> 01:05:08,975
- Yeah right, you'll never see him again.

1995
01:05:08,975 --> 01:05:09,808
- [Joel] Hey, this is great.

1996
01:05:09,808 --> 01:05:11,394
He looks like a canceled stamp.

1997
01:05:11,394 --> 01:05:13,506
(Crow chuckles)

1998
01:05:13,506 --> 01:05:17,256
(Tom sings along with score)

1999
01:05:19,234 --> 01:05:21,226
- Well, time for a drink. Yep.

2000
01:05:21,226 --> 01:05:22,893
- It's getting later and later.

2001
01:05:22,893 --> 01:05:24,844
Tammy? I think we'd better take off.

2002
01:05:24,844 --> 01:05:26,163
Ready?
- Yes, Captain!

2003
01:05:26,163 --> 01:05:27,684
- [Tom] Right.

2004
01:05:27,684 --> 01:05:29,154
- Flyin' high now.

2005
01:05:29,154 --> 01:05:29,987
You're into what?

2006
01:05:29,987 --> 01:05:31,063
- What?

2007
01:05:31,063 --> 01:05:32,554
Dan was trapped?

2008
01:05:32,554 --> 01:05:34,282
- Yes, I tried to help him, but--

2009
01:05:34,282 --> 01:05:36,103
- [Joel] He already
chewed half his leg off!

2010
01:05:36,103 --> 01:05:36,936
- [Tom] Ew.

2011
01:05:36,936 --> 01:05:38,123
- I heard what he said.

2012
01:05:38,123 --> 01:05:39,523
I can rescue Dan.

2013
01:05:39,523 --> 01:05:41,954
- Can you get him out
before the bomb goes off?

2014
01:05:41,954 --> 01:05:43,773
- I can try.

2015
01:05:43,773 --> 01:05:45,146
- We've gotta be sure.

2016
01:05:45,146 --> 01:05:47,612
- We'll never save Dan
by talking about it!

2017
01:05:47,612 --> 01:05:49,652
- [Tom] Well, then let's sing about it!

2018
01:05:49,652 --> 01:05:51,759
- Billy, you stop worrying.

2019
01:05:51,759 --> 01:05:52,850
(Tob sobs)
Okay.

2020
01:05:52,850 --> 01:05:53,831
- Thanks for cheering me up.

2021
01:05:53,831 --> 01:05:54,900
You're a pip!

2022
01:05:54,900 --> 01:05:56,780
- You guys better get outta here, quick.

2023
01:05:56,780 --> 01:05:58,762
- Nothin' doin'.

2024
01:05:58,762 --> 01:05:59,732
(grunts) I'm going with you.

2025
01:05:59,732 --> 01:06:01,040
- No, you're not!

2026
01:06:01,040 --> 01:06:02,882
You get back to the ship.

2027
01:06:02,882 --> 01:06:04,322
- I want to help you rescue Dan.

2028
01:06:04,322 --> 01:06:05,362
- [Joel] I want to know what love is.

2029
01:06:05,362 --> 01:06:08,991
- Your injured leg,
you'd only be in my way.

2030
01:06:08,991 --> 01:06:11,442
(pained grunting)
(device buzzing)

2031
01:06:11,442 --> 01:06:13,262
- This is great. Do we have to see this?

2032
01:06:13,262 --> 01:06:14,183
Come on.

2033
01:06:14,183 --> 01:06:15,501
- [Joel] Sounds like he's getting a tattoo

2034
01:06:15,501 --> 01:06:16,903
with the Bizzy Buzz Buzz or something.

2035
01:06:16,903 --> 01:06:18,142
- [Tom] Oh, Victor Kiam,

2036
01:06:18,142 --> 01:06:19,252
why did you have to buy the company?

2037
01:06:19,252 --> 01:06:22,650
- What is the nature of your mission here?

2038
01:06:22,650 --> 01:06:24,143
Huh?
(pained screaming)

2039
01:06:24,143 --> 01:06:26,101
- [Joel] Shaves like a blade! (grunts)

2040
01:06:26,101 --> 01:06:27,592
- [Tom] Or your money back.

2041
01:06:27,592 --> 01:06:29,112
- I'm going to have to drill again.

2042
01:06:29,112 --> 01:06:32,570
- You were collecting
information on our secret weapon.

2043
01:06:32,570 --> 01:06:34,000
You're a spy, aren't you?

2044
01:06:34,000 --> 01:06:35,130
Huh?

2045
01:06:35,130 --> 01:06:36,530
- [Tom] Now rinse, please.

2046
01:06:36,530 --> 01:06:37,363
Is it safe?

2047
01:06:37,363 --> 01:06:39,581
(device buzzing)

2048
01:06:39,581 --> 01:06:41,129
- Who sent you here?

2049
01:06:41,129 --> 01:06:43,450
- If you don't look
good, we don't look good.

2050
01:06:43,450 --> 01:06:44,889
(pained grunting)

2051
01:06:44,889 --> 01:06:48,077
See, you're not enjoying this.

2052
01:06:48,077 --> 01:06:51,318
Now I think you'd better answer us.

2053
01:06:51,318 --> 01:06:54,747
Otherwise, things will get even worse.

2054
01:06:54,747 --> 01:06:55,580
Huh?

2055
01:06:55,580 --> 01:06:57,217
- [Joel] Just a little
off the top! (grunts)

2056
01:06:57,217 --> 01:06:58,569
- [Interrogator] Talk! Talk!

2057
01:06:58,569 --> 01:07:00,108
- [Tom] Talk Talk by Talk Talk

2058
01:07:00,108 --> 01:07:02,097
from the album Talk Talk.

2059
01:07:02,097 --> 01:07:04,680
(engines boom)

2060
01:07:10,516 --> 01:07:11,689
Yup.

2061
01:07:11,689 --> 01:07:13,537
Fella could get rich flyin' a crop duster

2062
01:07:13,537 --> 01:07:18,028
if he lived long enough. (chuckles)

2063
01:07:18,028 --> 01:07:19,897
I don't think that was the best.

2064
01:07:19,897 --> 01:07:21,209
- [Joel] Man, should I be driving?

2065
01:07:21,209 --> 01:07:24,042
I mean, I've already got two DWIs.

2066
01:07:26,276 --> 01:07:27,465
(dramatic music)

2067
01:07:27,465 --> 01:07:29,518
(Crow chirps)

2068
01:07:29,518 --> 01:07:30,369
(gun fires)

2069
01:07:30,369 --> 01:07:31,587
- [Tom] Ooh.
(pained grunting)

2070
01:07:31,587 --> 01:07:32,688
- Oh! (chuckles)

2071
01:07:32,688 --> 01:07:33,860
Interpretive death.

2072
01:07:33,860 --> 01:07:35,167
Flip shot to a summersault!

2073
01:07:35,167 --> 01:07:37,198
Pretty routine, I've seen that before.

2074
01:07:37,198 --> 01:07:38,660
(grunting)

2075
01:07:38,660 --> 01:07:42,448
- [Joel] Hey, it's a three legged race!

2076
01:07:42,448 --> 01:07:43,540
- Or five.

2077
01:07:43,540 --> 01:07:44,373
- [Tom] Huh?

2078
01:07:44,373 --> 01:07:46,545
(beeping)

2079
01:07:46,545 --> 01:07:47,486
Oh, snaggletooth!

2080
01:07:47,486 --> 01:07:50,225
- [Tammy] Captain, they're
back on the screen!

2081
01:07:50,225 --> 01:07:51,487
- That's great.
(bots growl)

2082
01:07:51,487 --> 01:07:53,546
Didn't I tell you that
they were professionals?

2083
01:07:53,546 --> 01:07:55,336
- Yes, sir.
(men grunting)

2084
01:07:55,336 --> 01:07:56,806
- [Joel] Professional what?

2085
01:07:56,806 --> 01:07:57,776
- Is this dubbed?

2086
01:07:57,776 --> 01:07:58,954
It sounds like it might be dubbed.

2087
01:07:58,954 --> 01:08:02,725
- Pretty much I think.
- It's dubbed.

2088
01:08:02,725 --> 01:08:04,594
- Hey, time's running out! Hurry!

2089
01:08:04,594 --> 01:08:06,256
- There's only seven minutes left.

2090
01:08:06,256 --> 01:08:08,045
- I know that, you idiot!

2091
01:08:08,045 --> 01:08:09,056
- Dan's still in there!

2092
01:08:09,056 --> 01:08:10,424
- [Joel] And he's got
the keys to your van,

2093
01:08:10,424 --> 01:08:13,565
and his dad was gonna buy us a keg!

2094
01:08:13,565 --> 01:08:14,445
- [Tom] Here, you want a sandwich?

2095
01:08:14,445 --> 01:08:16,264
I got chicken salad and some
peanut butter and jelly.

2096
01:08:16,264 --> 01:08:17,904
- I didn't mean to yell at you.

2097
01:08:17,904 --> 01:08:19,662
- Rocky, it's all my fault.

2098
01:08:19,662 --> 01:08:22,093
I should never have abandoned him.

2099
01:08:22,093 --> 01:08:23,522
- It's no one's fault.

2100
01:08:23,522 --> 01:08:25,703
And if anyone can save him, it's Ken.

2101
01:08:25,703 --> 01:08:27,133
You did the right thing in getting help.

2102
01:08:27,133 --> 01:08:28,802
- Yeah, it's Ken's fault!

2103
01:08:28,802 --> 01:08:31,802
- Yeah.
- Now pull yourself together.

2104
01:08:33,353 --> 01:08:35,245
- Look at that!
(whooshing)

2105
01:08:35,245 --> 01:08:36,314
Over there!

2106
01:08:36,314 --> 01:08:38,314
- [Tom] Odd, that plane's dusting crops

2107
01:08:38,314 --> 01:08:40,379
where there ain't no crops!
- Just in time!

2108
01:08:40,379 --> 01:08:41,212
- Cool.

2109
01:08:47,240 --> 01:08:49,979
- [Interrogator] This is
your last chance, Earthling.

2110
01:08:49,979 --> 01:08:52,110
Now, who sent you here and why?

2111
01:08:52,110 --> 01:08:53,291
- [Joel] Now remember, the first blade

2112
01:08:53,291 --> 01:08:55,091
pulls the whisker out, capisce?

2113
01:08:55,091 --> 01:08:57,331
(pained grunting)
(buzzing)

2114
01:08:57,331 --> 01:08:59,559
- Weapon. (grunting)

2115
01:08:59,559 --> 01:09:00,392
- [Tom] What?

2116
01:09:00,392 --> 01:09:01,408
- [Torturer] Now we're getting somewhere.

2117
01:09:01,408 --> 01:09:03,448
Who sent you?
(pained grunting)

2118
01:09:03,448 --> 01:09:04,281
- [Tom] Oil can?

2119
01:09:04,281 --> 01:09:05,342
Did he say oil can?

2120
01:09:05,342 --> 01:09:07,688
- Increase the voltage!

2121
01:09:07,688 --> 01:09:09,190
How much do you think you can take?

2122
01:09:09,190 --> 01:09:10,328
- He's an electro-holic.

2123
01:09:10,328 --> 01:09:12,237
Ohm is too many and a
trillion isn't enough.

2124
01:09:12,237 --> 01:09:13,749
(Tom chuckles)

2125
01:09:13,749 --> 01:09:16,968
- [Tom] Ohm is the loneliest
number, you know. (chuckles)

2126
01:09:16,968 --> 01:09:18,277
- He fainted.

2127
01:09:18,277 --> 01:09:20,408
Hurry! All of you!

2128
01:09:20,408 --> 01:09:21,768
We've got to locate that bomb!

2129
01:09:21,768 --> 01:09:22,601
- Yes, sir. Come on, men!

2130
01:09:22,601 --> 01:09:24,008
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

2131
01:09:24,008 --> 01:09:25,440
- Oh, no, you don't!

2132
01:09:25,440 --> 01:09:26,273
Dan!
- Hm?

2133
01:09:26,273 --> 01:09:27,683
- [Tom] Van Damme and Van Damme

2134
01:09:27,683 --> 01:09:31,421
in Van Damme You All to Hell. (laughs)

2135
01:09:31,421 --> 01:09:32,621
Woo!

2136
01:09:32,621 --> 01:09:34,472
- Double dog Van Damme.

2137
01:09:34,472 --> 01:09:37,472
(grunting)

2138
01:09:37,472 --> 01:09:39,560
Oh, this is great, the director chooses

2139
01:09:39,560 --> 01:09:40,992
closeups for the action sequences.

2140
01:09:40,992 --> 01:09:42,790
- [Tom] (chuckles) Perfect.

2141
01:09:42,790 --> 01:09:44,872
- [Joel] Oh, great, they're still parking.

2142
01:09:44,872 --> 01:09:45,923
- [Tom] Boy.

2143
01:09:45,923 --> 01:09:47,756
- Hard to find a spot.

2144
01:09:50,392 --> 01:09:52,110
(wheezing)

2145
01:09:52,110 --> 01:09:53,651
- [Tom] They communicate by gasping.

2146
01:09:53,651 --> 01:09:56,270
(Tom mimics gasping)

2147
01:09:56,270 --> 01:09:58,171
- [Joel] Hey, look, Edelweiss.

2148
01:09:58,171 --> 01:09:59,004
- Pretty.

2149
01:10:02,529 --> 01:10:03,449
- Rocky, hurry!

2150
01:10:03,449 --> 01:10:04,282
- Again?

2151
01:10:05,280 --> 01:10:06,331
- Where's Ken and Dan?

2152
01:10:06,331 --> 01:10:07,570
- [Tom] That's a good
question, let's talk about it

2153
01:10:07,570 --> 01:10:08,539
on the way home.

2154
01:10:08,539 --> 01:10:11,262
- In five minutes, that bomb goes off.

2155
01:10:11,262 --> 01:10:12,884
And they're still in there.

2156
01:10:12,884 --> 01:10:14,852
We have to leave.

2157
01:10:14,852 --> 01:10:16,342
- Why are they still in there?

2158
01:10:16,342 --> 01:10:17,532
What's happened to Ken?

2159
01:10:17,532 --> 01:10:18,772
- [Joel] Ah, he's into Barbie.

2160
01:10:18,772 --> 01:10:20,189
It's sad, really.

2161
01:10:21,702 --> 01:10:23,592
- [Tom] But you're skirting
the whole Ken issue.

2162
01:10:23,592 --> 01:10:24,425
(worrying music)

2163
01:10:24,425 --> 01:10:26,762
- Every time I really like a guy.

2164
01:10:26,762 --> 01:10:30,017
(lasers fire)
(grunting)

2165
01:10:30,017 --> 01:10:30,945
- [Joel] You know, I love my work.

2166
01:10:30,945 --> 01:10:33,793
I never think I gotta go
to work, I just love it.

2167
01:10:33,793 --> 01:10:35,494
- [Tom] Oh.

2168
01:10:35,494 --> 01:10:36,764
(grunting)

2169
01:10:36,764 --> 01:10:40,525
Hi-keeba?
(grunting)

2170
01:10:40,525 --> 01:10:41,358
Hey!

2171
01:10:42,205 --> 01:10:43,443
Hi-keeba.

2172
01:10:43,443 --> 01:10:44,276
Nice dismount.

2173
01:10:44,276 --> 01:10:45,109
Gymkata!

2174
01:10:46,153 --> 01:10:47,153
Ho, hey, ho!

2175
01:10:49,172 --> 01:10:50,972
(shouting)

2176
01:10:50,972 --> 01:10:52,055
Gymkata! Hai!

2177
01:10:53,543 --> 01:10:54,652
Ah, it's fun.

2178
01:10:54,652 --> 01:10:56,692
(grunting and shouting)

2179
01:10:56,692 --> 01:10:57,692
- Hm.
- Say.

2180
01:11:00,043 --> 01:11:01,213
- [Tom] Good one.

2181
01:11:01,213 --> 01:11:02,364
- [Ken] Huh-shick!

2182
01:11:02,364 --> 01:11:04,854
- [Tom] What did, Ken!

2183
01:11:04,854 --> 01:11:06,354
- Easy, that's it!

2184
01:11:07,562 --> 01:11:08,395
- [Tom] Easy does it.

2185
01:11:08,395 --> 01:11:10,592
- [Joel] I'm serious about mufflers.

2186
01:11:10,592 --> 01:11:11,451
(Tom chuckles)

2187
01:11:11,451 --> 01:11:12,779
- Three minutes till the explosion.

2188
01:11:12,779 --> 01:11:14,220
- I can get in a quick one.

2189
01:11:14,220 --> 01:11:17,432
- [Tom] Yeah, we gotta get
in a quick one, too, guys.

2190
01:11:17,432 --> 01:11:18,491
- Please, wait, sir.

2191
01:11:18,491 --> 01:11:21,574
Ken and Dan can't be that far away.

2192
01:11:21,574 --> 01:11:23,312
(worrying music)

2193
01:11:23,312 --> 01:11:24,854
(panting)

2194
01:11:24,854 --> 01:11:26,104
Ken!

2195
01:11:26,104 --> 01:11:27,104
Ken made it!

2196
01:11:36,203 --> 01:11:37,774
- [Tom] All right, I'm
feelin' really good!

2197
01:11:37,774 --> 01:11:39,214
- Yeah.
- Oh, boy!

2198
01:11:39,214 --> 01:11:43,203
♪ This is the song
starting off our medley ♪

2199
01:11:43,203 --> 01:11:47,412
♪ Our favorite Fugitive Alien songs ♪

2200
01:11:47,412 --> 01:11:50,853
♪ Don't try to kill us with a forklift ♪

2201
01:11:50,853 --> 01:11:52,722
♪ It won't take very long ♪

2202
01:11:52,722 --> 01:11:55,972
♪ Relax and sing along ♪

2203
01:11:57,002 --> 01:11:57,835
- Thank you, thank you.

2204
01:11:57,835 --> 01:12:00,423
- You know, Tommy, a
movie like Fugitive Alien

2205
01:12:00,423 --> 01:12:01,710
can make you cry,

2206
01:12:01,710 --> 01:12:03,602
and it can make you cry.
- Ah me, yes.

2207
01:12:03,602 --> 01:12:04,799
- But the thing I treasure most,

2208
01:12:04,799 --> 01:12:05,983
and I'm speaking from the heart here,

2209
01:12:05,983 --> 01:12:07,293
this is totally off script--

2210
01:12:07,293 --> 01:12:08,361
- Mm-hmm.
- Is the music.

2211
01:12:08,361 --> 01:12:09,703
- Oh, this is so true, mon Crow.

2212
01:12:09,703 --> 01:12:11,231
Songs of love an adventure,

2213
01:12:11,231 --> 01:12:13,551
and if I may, whimsy, no? (chuckles)

2214
01:12:13,551 --> 01:12:15,770
But you know, my favorite
was the heartrending ballad

2215
01:12:15,770 --> 01:12:18,959
in which the wistful Tammy
pledges her love to Ken.

2216
01:12:18,959 --> 01:12:21,711
- It goes a little something like this.

2217
01:12:21,711 --> 01:12:24,061
(clears throat)
- Two, three, four.

2218
01:12:24,061 --> 01:12:27,799
♪ I love Ken, he is my sweet friend ♪

2219
01:12:27,799 --> 01:12:29,740
♪ And I love him ♪
♪ I love Ken ♪

2220
01:12:29,740 --> 01:12:31,779
♪ He is my sweet friend ♪

2221
01:12:31,779 --> 01:12:33,781
♪ And I love him ♪
♪ I'm so blue ♪

2222
01:12:33,781 --> 01:12:36,399
♪ 'Cause I don't think Ken loves me ♪

2223
01:12:36,399 --> 01:12:37,859
♪ I'm so blue ♪

2224
01:12:37,859 --> 01:12:40,530
♪ 'cause I don't think Ken loves me ♪

2225
01:12:40,530 --> 01:12:42,923
♪ I'm all messed up inside ♪

2226
01:12:42,923 --> 01:12:44,843
♪ I might have to off him ♪

2227
01:12:44,843 --> 01:12:47,283
♪ I'm all messed up inside ♪

2228
01:12:47,283 --> 01:12:49,303
♪ I might have to off him ♪

2229
01:12:49,303 --> 01:12:50,525
♪ I'll frame Rocky ♪

2230
01:12:50,525 --> 01:12:52,902
♪ And get away Scott free ♪

2231
01:12:52,902 --> 01:12:57,222
♪ I'll frame Rocky and
get away Scott free ♪

2232
01:12:57,222 --> 01:13:01,181
♪ I love Ken, he is my sweet
friend, and I love him ♪

2233
01:13:01,181 --> 01:13:05,132
(Tom sings in foreign language)

2234
01:13:05,132 --> 01:13:10,132
♪ I'm so blue 'cause I
don't think Ken loves me ♪

2235
01:13:13,302 --> 01:13:15,741
♪ I'm all missed up inside ♪

2236
01:13:15,741 --> 01:13:17,352
♪ I might have to off him ♪

2237
01:13:17,352 --> 01:13:19,062
♪ I saw three ships come sailing in ♪

2238
01:13:19,062 --> 01:13:21,443
♪ On Christmas day, on Christmas day ♪

2239
01:13:21,443 --> 01:13:25,814
♪ I'll frame Rocky and
get away Scott free ♪

2240
01:13:25,814 --> 01:13:29,592
♪ I love Ken, I love Ken ♪

2241
01:13:29,592 --> 01:13:32,202
- All right, this band is marvelous!

2242
01:13:32,202 --> 01:13:33,444
Aren't they ladies and gentlemen?

2243
01:13:33,444 --> 01:13:35,984
Cambot Brown and his band renown!

2244
01:13:35,984 --> 01:13:37,046
Give it up for 'em!

2245
01:13:37,046 --> 01:13:39,286
(upbeat jazzy music)
- Yeah!

2246
01:13:39,286 --> 01:13:40,241
- Smokin'.
- Yeah!

2247
01:13:40,241 --> 01:13:41,362
- One, two, three.

2248
01:13:41,362 --> 01:13:43,561
♪ It's got a real cool feel ♪

2249
01:13:43,561 --> 01:13:44,782
(Tom scats)

2250
01:13:44,782 --> 01:13:46,979
♪ Flying high with Star Wolf ♪

2251
01:13:46,979 --> 01:13:48,179
- Hah!

2252
01:13:48,179 --> 01:13:51,467
♪ We're firin' up the ship ♪

2253
01:13:51,467 --> 01:13:53,907
♪ And we're hittin' the town ♪

2254
01:13:53,907 --> 01:13:54,740
- Boogie, boogie!

2255
01:13:54,740 --> 01:13:57,078
♪ With groovy Ken and Tammy ♪

2256
01:13:57,078 --> 01:13:58,198
- Yeah! Hah!

2257
01:13:58,198 --> 01:14:01,587
♪ Swingin' Rocky and Joe ♪

2258
01:14:01,587 --> 01:14:04,787
♪ And there's two other guys
who we don't really know ♪

2259
01:14:04,787 --> 01:14:07,059
♪ Forget 'em, lay down the boogie ♪

2260
01:14:07,059 --> 01:14:09,699
♪ And head for the stars, man ♪

2261
01:14:09,699 --> 01:14:10,787
- Thanks, Joel.

2262
01:14:10,787 --> 01:14:12,488
Oh, that was fun.

2263
01:14:12,488 --> 01:14:14,297
But if I can get a little
serous for a moment,

2264
01:14:14,297 --> 01:14:16,126
well, I was wondering where we'd be

2265
01:14:16,126 --> 01:14:19,155
without our boys and girls
in shiny red pleather.

2266
01:14:19,155 --> 01:14:23,947
It makes me proud to know that
they're out there somewhere.

2267
01:14:23,947 --> 01:14:27,737
♪ Look and you see, flying so fancy free ♪

2268
01:14:27,737 --> 01:14:29,846
♪ Fighting for you and me ♪

2269
01:14:29,846 --> 01:14:32,838
♪ Captain Joe and the gang ♪

2270
01:14:32,838 --> 01:14:34,446
♪ When they pass by ♪

2271
01:14:34,446 --> 01:14:36,627
♪ Feel it in pumpkin pie ♪

2272
01:14:36,627 --> 01:14:38,204
♪ Tenth in the neck would die ♪

2273
01:14:38,204 --> 01:14:39,695
- Tempo.
♪ Return the blue ♪

2274
01:14:39,695 --> 01:14:41,386
- Tempo.
- That's really good, Gypsy.

2275
01:14:41,386 --> 01:14:42,884
- Do you wanna do one with me?

2276
01:14:42,884 --> 01:14:43,717
- Huh?

2277
01:14:43,717 --> 01:14:44,604
- Do you wanna do one with me?

2278
01:14:44,604 --> 01:14:45,437
- Oh, what?

2279
01:14:45,437 --> 01:14:46,270
- Let's all do it.
- Okay.

2280
01:14:46,270 --> 01:14:49,895
♪ We're are gonna find Sandy Frank ♪

2281
01:14:49,895 --> 01:14:54,895
♪ We just wanna him why ♪

2282
01:14:55,067 --> 01:14:59,287
♪ We wanna stick it to Sandy Frank ♪

2283
01:14:59,287 --> 01:15:01,496
♪ And sit on his chest
and gob on his face ♪

2284
01:15:01,496 --> 01:15:04,413
♪ And make him cry ♪

2285
01:15:06,407 --> 01:15:08,458
- Yeah!
- That's right, take it home!

2286
01:15:08,458 --> 01:15:09,746
- I'm feelin' really good!

2287
01:15:09,746 --> 01:15:11,178
- Feels so good it shows!

2288
01:15:11,178 --> 01:15:12,964
- Yeah, yeah!
- Yeah!

2289
01:15:12,964 --> 01:15:13,844
- Two, three.

2290
01:15:13,844 --> 01:15:15,244
♪ And that's our song ♪

2291
01:15:15,244 --> 01:15:17,716
♪ We hope that you enjoyed it ♪

2292
01:15:17,716 --> 01:15:21,986
♪ And if you thought that
it was stupid and trite ♪

2293
01:15:21,986 --> 01:15:25,694
♪ Come on and kill us with a forklift ♪

2294
01:15:25,694 --> 01:15:30,574
♪ All we wanna do, with
love from us to you ♪

2295
01:15:30,574 --> 01:15:33,794
♪ Is sing ♪

2296
01:15:33,794 --> 01:15:37,294
♪ The Fugitive Alien song ♪

2297
01:15:38,684 --> 01:15:40,135
- Muah!
- Yah, huh, huh!

2298
01:15:40,135 --> 01:15:40,968
- Hi-keeba!

2299
01:15:40,968 --> 01:15:44,051
(upbeat theme music)

2300
01:15:47,856 --> 01:15:49,776
- [Tom] No, no, you are Mr. Show Business.

2301
01:15:49,776 --> 01:15:50,973
(cross-talking)

2302
01:15:50,973 --> 01:15:52,295
- Smokin'.

2303
01:15:52,295 --> 01:15:54,174
- [Tom] Absolutely.

2304
01:15:54,174 --> 01:15:56,236
- Catchy.
(explosion booms)

2305
01:15:56,236 --> 01:15:57,894
- [Tom] Ooh.

2306
01:15:57,894 --> 01:15:59,025
Oh, no!

2307
01:15:59,025 --> 01:16:00,305
- Hey.

2308
01:16:00,305 --> 01:16:02,463
- [Tom] That big Mega
Servo just went up there.

2309
01:16:02,463 --> 01:16:04,574
- [Joel] Oh, no.

2310
01:16:04,574 --> 01:16:05,634
- [Tom] Doggone it.

2311
01:16:05,634 --> 01:16:07,242
- Oh, they blewed it up

2312
01:16:07,242 --> 01:16:09,624
before we found out what it was!

2313
01:16:09,624 --> 01:16:11,813
- Blewed?
- Blewed it up.

2314
01:16:11,813 --> 01:16:13,743
- [Tom] Now you see, this is
why we don't let teenagers

2315
01:16:13,743 --> 01:16:15,942
into hotels anymore.

2316
01:16:15,942 --> 01:16:17,042
This kinda stuff.

2317
01:16:17,042 --> 01:16:18,144
- [Crow] Especially New Kids.

2318
01:16:18,144 --> 01:16:19,323
- [Tom] Mm.

2319
01:16:19,323 --> 01:16:20,694
- (gasps) Look.
- Huh?

2320
01:16:20,694 --> 01:16:21,527
- Sir!

2321
01:16:22,475 --> 01:16:23,475
- All right!

2322
01:16:24,843 --> 01:16:26,402
(Joel chuckles mockingly)

2323
01:16:26,402 --> 01:16:27,242
- Terrific!

2324
01:16:27,242 --> 01:16:28,733
- Super, really super!

2325
01:16:28,733 --> 01:16:31,566
(explosions boom)

2326
01:16:33,453 --> 01:16:34,286
- Here it goes!

2327
01:16:34,286 --> 01:16:35,352
- [Tom] All right.

2328
01:16:35,352 --> 01:16:36,891
Ah, cherry, bar, cherry.

2329
01:16:36,891 --> 01:16:38,813
I haven't won all day.

2330
01:16:38,813 --> 01:16:41,646
(explosion booms)

2331
01:16:43,281 --> 01:16:45,482
- [Joel] We never found out
how big that thing was really.

2332
01:16:45,482 --> 01:16:46,315
- No.

2333
01:16:46,315 --> 01:16:48,482
- [Tom] No relative scale.

2334
01:16:50,832 --> 01:16:52,864
Wait, wait, what was the plot here?

2335
01:16:52,864 --> 01:16:54,485
I think they blew that up, too.

2336
01:16:54,485 --> 01:16:56,353
(Tom chuckles)

2337
01:16:56,353 --> 01:16:58,524
- It's Fahrvergnügen gone horribly wrong.

2338
01:16:58,524 --> 01:16:59,941
- [Tom] I'll say.

2339
01:17:01,313 --> 01:17:03,480
(snoring)

2340
01:17:06,205 --> 01:17:08,133
Know what this reminds me of?

2341
01:17:08,133 --> 01:17:10,373
Thunderbirds are go!
- Yup.

2342
01:17:10,373 --> 01:17:11,853
- [Tom] (chuckles) Remember?

2343
01:17:11,853 --> 01:17:13,186
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

2344
01:17:15,053 --> 01:17:16,886
- That looks familiar.

2345
01:17:18,482 --> 01:17:20,704
- [Joel] Hey, do they have
another Herb Albert tape?

2346
01:17:20,704 --> 01:17:22,384
I'm really getting sick of this.

2347
01:17:22,384 --> 01:17:25,472
- [Tom] No, their 8-track recycled again.

2348
01:17:25,472 --> 01:17:27,333
- [Joel] You know, that
really does look good, though.

2349
01:17:27,333 --> 01:17:30,333
- It looks neat.
- Pretty impressive.

2350
01:17:35,322 --> 01:17:36,733
- Did Kissinger order this?

2351
01:17:36,733 --> 01:17:37,802
- [Tom] I think it was Schwarzkopf.

2352
01:17:37,802 --> 01:17:38,635
- Oh.

2353
01:17:41,762 --> 01:17:43,592
- [Joel] So there's stuff blowing up then.

2354
01:17:43,592 --> 01:17:45,112
- Pretty much.
- It's pretty neat.

2355
01:17:45,112 --> 01:17:47,133
- Kinda neat, yup.
- Yup.

2356
01:17:47,133 --> 01:17:48,413
- Blowin' it up.
- Yup.

2357
01:17:48,413 --> 01:17:49,453
- Yupper-doodle-doo.

2358
01:17:49,453 --> 01:17:50,613
- [Tom] Had some money to blow here.

2359
01:17:50,613 --> 01:17:51,530
- Oh, yeah.

2360
01:17:52,765 --> 01:17:54,405
- [Tom] (chuckles) It's sprinkle.

2361
01:17:54,405 --> 01:17:55,624
- [Joel] It does look good, though.

2362
01:17:55,624 --> 01:17:57,434
- Yeah, great.
- Really good.

2363
01:17:57,434 --> 01:17:59,593
- [Tom] Orgy of destruction,
always kinda fun.

2364
01:17:59,593 --> 01:18:01,274
- Sorry, everyone! Sorry!

2365
01:18:01,274 --> 01:18:02,944
Only meant to blow up that one thing.

2366
01:18:02,944 --> 01:18:03,853
Sorry.

2367
01:18:03,853 --> 01:18:06,013
- [Joel] It's the bridge on
the River Kwai over there.

2368
01:18:06,013 --> 01:18:09,324
(Tom whistles)

2369
01:18:09,324 --> 01:18:10,907
- Lower the bridge.

2370
01:18:14,042 --> 01:18:15,594
- [Tom] Yup.

2371
01:18:15,594 --> 01:18:16,771
- And they still haven't hit that.

2372
01:18:16,771 --> 01:18:18,854
- [Tom] Oh, here it goes.

2373
01:18:19,762 --> 01:18:20,595
Wuh-oh.

2374
01:18:21,932 --> 01:18:25,114
Next on MacGyver. (chuckles)

2375
01:18:25,114 --> 01:18:26,572
- Can't begin to tell you how proud

2376
01:18:26,572 --> 01:18:28,324
I am of you guys.
- 'Cause I'm drunk.

2377
01:18:28,324 --> 01:18:31,241
- Greatest crew a captain ever had.

2378
01:18:32,372 --> 01:18:33,621
(Tom chuckles mockingly)

2379
01:18:33,621 --> 01:18:35,914
- He's all right.
- Hey, Ken.

2380
01:18:35,914 --> 01:18:36,747
- Hm?

2381
01:18:36,747 --> 01:18:37,724
- [Joel] Pull my finger,

2382
01:18:37,724 --> 01:18:40,301
then do that funny face you do.

2383
01:18:40,301 --> 01:18:41,572
(chuckles)
(Tom chuckles mockingly)

2384
01:18:41,572 --> 01:18:43,602
- [Joel] Ha ha! Yeah.

2385
01:18:43,602 --> 01:18:44,562
- [Tom] Pull my finger, too.

2386
01:18:44,562 --> 01:18:47,622
I love it when they do that.

2387
01:18:47,622 --> 01:18:48,871
- See, it's all workin' out.

2388
01:18:48,871 --> 01:18:51,580
I wish your mother were here to see this.

2389
01:18:51,580 --> 01:18:53,180
(Tom sighs)

2390
01:18:53,180 --> 01:18:54,013
Hmm.

2391
01:18:55,791 --> 01:18:56,624
- [Tom] So--
(Joel yelps)

2392
01:18:56,624 --> 01:18:57,900
- Rangers!

2393
01:18:57,900 --> 01:18:59,650
- [Tom] Gene Simmons?

2394
01:19:00,610 --> 01:19:02,908
- A research center on Earth

2395
01:19:02,908 --> 01:19:05,708
has just developed a bomb that
can destroy a whole planet.

2396
01:19:05,708 --> 01:19:07,708
- And you guys can't cut a
simple stake and shrimp combo.

2397
01:19:07,708 --> 01:19:09,527
- We will gain control of that bomb,

2398
01:19:09,527 --> 01:19:11,727
and then Valna will dominate the universe.

2399
01:19:11,727 --> 01:19:13,309
- [Goons] Yes, master!

2400
01:19:13,309 --> 01:19:15,178
- [Joel] The University
of Wisconsin, Madison,

2401
01:19:15,178 --> 01:19:17,206
a traditional of excellence
for over 200 years.

2402
01:19:17,206 --> 01:19:19,217
- I've been waiting for you, Captain.

2403
01:19:19,217 --> 01:19:21,825
- Five neat guys and a girl.
- That's not very wise.

2404
01:19:21,825 --> 01:19:23,446
- We're at the Reynold's aluminum plant.

2405
01:19:23,446 --> 01:19:24,905
- It's too dangerous.

2406
01:19:24,905 --> 01:19:26,944
- [Woman] I'm sorry,
my father was detained.

2407
01:19:26,944 --> 01:19:30,046
- What?
- He wanted to welcome you.

2408
01:19:30,046 --> 01:19:31,595
- Mother!
- Hm?

2409
01:19:31,595 --> 01:19:32,892
- What?
- What's up, Ken?

2410
01:19:32,892 --> 01:19:34,094
- Who is that?
- He's tripping.

2411
01:19:34,094 --> 01:19:35,543
- Looked like my mother.

2412
01:19:35,543 --> 01:19:36,843
Why'd she run away?

2413
01:19:36,843 --> 01:19:38,014
- 'Cause she hated kids, maybe?

2414
01:19:38,014 --> 01:19:39,264
- Mother!
- Ooh.

2415
01:19:40,770 --> 01:19:42,879
- Hey, not so fast, Ken!

2416
01:19:42,879 --> 01:19:44,481
Take it easy.

2417
01:19:44,481 --> 01:19:46,082
You know you you haven't
seen her in several years.

2418
01:19:46,082 --> 01:19:48,762
- [Joel] Sounds like they're
playing the Godfather theme.

2419
01:19:48,762 --> 01:19:50,743
- But no one ever really proved it.

2420
01:19:50,743 --> 01:19:51,576
That's why I--

2421
01:19:51,576 --> 01:19:53,050
- Ken, snap out of it.

2422
01:19:53,050 --> 01:19:54,289
- [Tom] Come on, this is your mother now.

2423
01:19:54,289 --> 01:19:55,122
Try her out.

2424
01:19:55,122 --> 01:19:58,452
- We've been assigned to
escort this young lady.

2425
01:19:58,452 --> 01:20:00,343
- I beg your pardon.

2426
01:20:00,343 --> 01:20:01,671
- Hi-keeba.
- That's all right.

2427
01:20:01,671 --> 01:20:03,761
- The problem is my father.

2428
01:20:03,761 --> 01:20:05,751
Ever since he developed that bomb,

2429
01:20:05,751 --> 01:20:09,751
all sorts of people have
been threatening me.

2430
01:20:09,751 --> 01:20:10,962
- Look, sir.

2431
01:20:10,962 --> 01:20:12,442
(dramatic menacing music)
- [Tom] Huh?

2432
01:20:12,442 --> 01:20:13,275
Uh-oh.

2433
01:20:14,663 --> 01:20:18,042
- [Joel] We're being attacked
by models from Members Only!

2434
01:20:18,042 --> 01:20:19,270
(Tom sings along with score)

2435
01:20:19,270 --> 01:20:20,510
- [Rocky] Take cover!

2436
01:20:20,510 --> 01:20:22,592
(lasers fire)

2437
01:20:22,592 --> 01:20:23,563
- [Tom] Oh, no.

2438
01:20:23,563 --> 01:20:25,350
It's the Dave Clark Five
and they're being attacked

2439
01:20:25,350 --> 01:20:27,433
by Dino, Desi, and Billy!

2440
01:20:28,832 --> 01:20:30,453
- It's like one of those Obsession ads.

2441
01:20:30,453 --> 01:20:33,003
- [Tom] If this is love,
then find me guilty.

2442
01:20:33,003 --> 01:20:34,532
- Pretentious and dull.

2443
01:20:34,532 --> 01:20:35,782
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

2444
01:20:37,183 --> 01:20:39,503
- [Joel] Hey, it's the
guys from Delta Epsilon!

2445
01:20:39,503 --> 01:20:41,732
- [Tom] Against the guys from Sigma Phi.

2446
01:20:41,732 --> 01:20:43,682
- This kinda stuff
always happens on campus.

2447
01:20:43,682 --> 01:20:44,681
- [Tom] Yeah.

2448
01:20:44,681 --> 01:20:47,503
- Those soldiers moved
faster than I expected.

2449
01:20:47,503 --> 01:20:48,336
- Yeah.

2450
01:20:49,346 --> 01:20:50,836
- [Tom] Guido Sarducci?

2451
01:20:50,836 --> 01:20:52,426
- The manufacture of my invention.

2452
01:20:52,426 --> 01:20:53,287
- [Joel] Sugar in this gum?

2453
01:20:53,287 --> 01:20:54,796
- Preserved on this microfilm.

2454
01:20:54,796 --> 01:20:57,927
- [Tom] So it doesn't
stick to dental work, eh?

2455
01:20:57,927 --> 01:21:00,087
- You mean this little film--
- Mm-hmm.

2456
01:21:00,087 --> 01:21:01,495
- Contains information on a bomb

2457
01:21:01,495 --> 01:21:03,935
powerful enough to blow
up the entire universe?

2458
01:21:03,935 --> 01:21:06,026
- No matter what happens to me, Captain,

2459
01:21:06,026 --> 01:21:08,135
this microfilm must not
fall into the wrong hands.

2460
01:21:08,135 --> 01:21:09,524
- Why are they meeting in the shower?

2461
01:21:09,524 --> 01:21:11,564
- Not to make this invention public.

2462
01:21:11,564 --> 01:21:14,964
- [Joel] By the way, you're
sitting on the urinal.

2463
01:21:14,964 --> 01:21:16,733
(Tom hums casually)

2464
01:21:16,733 --> 01:21:18,975
- Tammy's got a Weber cooker.
- There she is again!

2465
01:21:18,975 --> 01:21:21,642
(curious music)

2466
01:21:23,242 --> 01:21:24,095
- Mother!

2467
01:21:24,095 --> 01:21:25,474
Why does she always run away?

2468
01:21:25,474 --> 01:21:28,404
- [Tom] And why is she younger than me?

2469
01:21:28,404 --> 01:21:29,237
Uh-oh.

2470
01:21:30,603 --> 01:21:32,843
- [Joel] Oh, man, now he's outside.

2471
01:21:32,843 --> 01:21:34,093
I'd see this part of the movie

2472
01:21:34,093 --> 01:21:35,914
needs a strict rewrite.

2473
01:21:35,914 --> 01:21:36,923
- [Tom] It's a little weird.

2474
01:21:36,923 --> 01:21:37,756
- Hey, Mom!

2475
01:21:37,756 --> 01:21:40,735
Where'd ya get the meadow?

2476
01:21:40,735 --> 01:21:42,786
- [Tom] We're the catering squad.

2477
01:21:42,786 --> 01:21:44,026
Hi-keeba.

2478
01:21:44,026 --> 01:21:45,923
- Greetings from our headquarters.

2479
01:21:45,923 --> 01:21:47,682
We have orders to bring you there.

2480
01:21:47,682 --> 01:21:50,233
(grunting)
(worrying music)

2481
01:21:50,233 --> 01:21:51,802
- The captain's sportin'
a bike rack there.

2482
01:21:51,802 --> 01:21:53,933
- [Tom] Ooh! (chuckles)

2483
01:21:53,933 --> 01:21:55,935
- Tell your headquarters
they can forget their orders.

2484
01:21:55,935 --> 01:21:56,768
- Captain!

2485
01:21:59,268 --> 01:22:01,924
- [Joel] Ash Wednesday, Saysar style.

2486
01:22:01,924 --> 01:22:03,156
- [Tom] Dum dum!

2487
01:22:03,156 --> 01:22:03,989
- Ouch.

2488
01:22:05,533 --> 01:22:07,164
Filmed in Convolution-vision!

2489
01:22:07,164 --> 01:22:08,266
- [Tom] (chuckles) I'll say.

2490
01:22:08,266 --> 01:22:10,476
(panting)

2491
01:22:10,476 --> 01:22:13,059
(ship soaring)

2492
01:22:17,386 --> 01:22:18,679
- Oh, ah!
- Mother, come back!

2493
01:22:18,679 --> 01:22:21,130
- What in the Sam Scratch is goin' on?

2494
01:22:21,130 --> 01:22:22,519
- [Tom] This is an
entirely different movie

2495
01:22:22,519 --> 01:22:24,060
we're watching here.

2496
01:22:24,060 --> 01:22:25,997
- It was Halkon.

2497
01:22:25,997 --> 01:22:27,359
- [Tom] Who?

2498
01:22:27,359 --> 01:22:29,119
Fred Biletnikoff!
- Attack.

2499
01:22:29,119 --> 01:22:31,536
(beams fire)

2500
01:22:32,698 --> 01:22:35,119
- [Joel] Hey, this side
shoots to the left.

2501
01:22:35,119 --> 01:22:37,369
- [Tom] Yup, heavily sided.

2502
01:22:41,349 --> 01:22:42,298
- Ken.

2503
01:22:42,298 --> 01:22:43,359
- Where the hell did you come from?

2504
01:22:43,359 --> 01:22:45,439
- All three of them were
to be taken back to Valna.

2505
01:22:45,439 --> 01:22:46,740
- Valna?
- Get me a spoon.

2506
01:22:46,740 --> 01:22:49,730
- Halkon was going to
hold them as hostages.

2507
01:22:49,730 --> 01:22:50,730
Just a minute.

2508
01:22:50,730 --> 01:22:52,218
This lady can tell you the rest.

2509
01:22:52,218 --> 01:22:53,370
- [Tom] The rest of the story.

2510
01:22:53,370 --> 01:22:54,440
- Halkon made me do it.
- Page two.

2511
01:22:54,440 --> 01:22:56,270
- He wanted me to
infiltrate your operation

2512
01:22:56,270 --> 01:22:58,880
posing as Ken's mother!

2513
01:22:58,880 --> 01:23:01,057
- Then he was going to kill her.

2514
01:23:01,057 --> 01:23:03,720
- It's like Oedipus.
- I better pay Halkon a visit.

2515
01:23:03,720 --> 01:23:05,640
(sobbing)

2516
01:23:05,640 --> 01:23:06,806
- Ken.

2517
01:23:06,806 --> 01:23:07,875
- You're not going to Valna.

2518
01:23:07,875 --> 01:23:09,603
- Dressed like that.
- That's crazy!

2519
01:23:09,603 --> 01:23:11,325
- He's right, Ken!

2520
01:23:11,325 --> 01:23:12,875
- What other choice do I have?

2521
01:23:12,875 --> 01:23:16,074
- You could get a smaller belt buckle.

2522
01:23:16,074 --> 01:23:16,952
- No way.

2523
01:23:16,952 --> 01:23:17,785
- [Joel And Bots] Jose.

2524
01:23:17,785 --> 01:23:18,912
- It's gotta be me.

2525
01:23:18,912 --> 01:23:20,754
♪ It's just gotta be me ♪

2526
01:23:20,754 --> 01:23:22,674
- Accept no responsibility.

2527
01:23:22,674 --> 01:23:24,874
You'd be acting on your own, Ken.

2528
01:23:24,874 --> 01:23:26,484
All we can do is wish you good luck.

2529
01:23:26,484 --> 01:23:28,924
- [Joel] Maybe pack you a few
sandwiches, but that's it.

2530
01:23:28,924 --> 01:23:29,757
- [Tom] That'd be nice.

2531
01:23:29,757 --> 01:23:33,373
- He must be destroyed by a Star Wolf!

2532
01:23:33,373 --> 01:23:34,933
- You'll always be a Star Wolf.

2533
01:23:34,933 --> 01:23:36,362
- But never a star.

2534
01:23:36,362 --> 01:23:37,592
(Ken laughs)

2535
01:23:37,592 --> 01:23:39,482
- Is that so awful?

2536
01:23:39,482 --> 01:23:41,952
If I'm able to use my
strength for a good cause?

2537
01:23:41,952 --> 01:23:44,562
- I'm just doin' what
Jerry does for those kids!

2538
01:23:44,562 --> 01:23:45,589
- Don't be a fool.

2539
01:23:45,589 --> 01:23:47,253
- [Joel] Don't be a fool
with your life, Billy.

2540
01:23:47,253 --> 01:23:48,880
- Nobody admires me more than I do.

2541
01:23:48,880 --> 01:23:49,713
- [Tom] Billy's over there.

2542
01:23:49,713 --> 01:23:51,792
- But you're no match for Halkon.

2543
01:23:51,792 --> 01:23:53,072
- Don't be so sure.

2544
01:23:53,072 --> 01:23:55,602
Halkon trained me for
every sort of combat.

2545
01:23:55,602 --> 01:23:57,162
He taught me well.

2546
01:23:57,162 --> 01:23:58,762
- One thing that Halkon didn't teach you

2547
01:23:58,762 --> 01:24:01,202
was to fight as dirty as he does,

2548
01:24:01,202 --> 01:24:03,141
which is the reason why

2549
01:24:03,141 --> 01:24:04,912
you'd better take some Earthlings along.

2550
01:24:04,912 --> 01:24:06,332
- [Joel] 'Cause we're basically scum.

2551
01:24:06,332 --> 01:24:07,961
- That's exactly what I was thinking.

2552
01:24:07,961 --> 01:24:11,044
(upbeat theme music)

2553
01:24:14,180 --> 01:24:16,598
- [Tom] I wonder what the
king is drinking tonight.

2554
01:24:16,598 --> 01:24:18,418
(urgent music)
(panting)

2555
01:24:18,418 --> 01:24:22,140
(Tom pants mockingly)

2556
01:24:22,140 --> 01:24:23,689
Oh, another Orrin Hatch.

2557
01:24:23,689 --> 01:24:25,149
- No, this one's a Richard Hatch.

2558
01:24:25,149 --> 01:24:25,982
- [Tom] Oh!

2559
01:24:25,982 --> 01:24:28,679
(bots giggle)

2560
01:24:28,679 --> 01:24:30,047
- One wretched Star Wolf?

2561
01:24:30,047 --> 01:24:33,009
- [Joel] Two wretched Star Wolves?

2562
01:24:33,009 --> 01:24:34,729
- I don't see any danger in that.

2563
01:24:34,729 --> 01:24:37,312
He had a space escort with him?

2564
01:24:38,759 --> 01:24:40,037
What's become of the others?

2565
01:24:40,037 --> 01:24:44,348
- Well, we're trying
to locate them, master.

2566
01:24:44,348 --> 01:24:46,929
- He's cute.
- I want Watford dead!

2567
01:24:46,929 --> 01:24:48,401
- Every one of them!

2568
01:24:48,401 --> 01:24:50,281
If they're not dead by
nightfall, you'll die!

2569
01:24:50,281 --> 01:24:52,864
- Yes, master!
- Oh, he is cute.

2570
01:24:54,151 --> 01:24:56,441
- [Tom] Kinda looks like
Tammy Faye, I think.

2571
01:24:56,441 --> 01:24:57,898
- Star Wolf.

2572
01:24:57,898 --> 01:24:59,111
(groans)

2573
01:24:59,111 --> 01:25:01,685
(grunting)

2574
01:25:01,685 --> 01:25:03,646
- Looking for me?

2575
01:25:03,646 --> 01:25:05,757
(bots chuckle)

2576
01:25:05,757 --> 01:25:07,197
Hello, Star Wolf.

2577
01:25:07,197 --> 01:25:08,186
- Hello, Shirl.

2578
01:25:08,186 --> 01:25:09,019
- Halkon.

2579
01:25:10,287 --> 01:25:12,717
I promised I'd return
here to settle the score.

2580
01:25:12,717 --> 01:25:14,375
- [Joel] Uh, I believe it was 15-love?

2581
01:25:14,375 --> 01:25:15,567
Something like that?

2582
01:25:15,567 --> 01:25:17,426
- Don't move!

2583
01:25:17,426 --> 01:25:18,346
(chuckles)

2584
01:25:18,346 --> 01:25:19,905
(Tom chuckles)

2585
01:25:19,905 --> 01:25:22,447
- You know you can't
bring ourself to kill me.

2586
01:25:22,447 --> 01:25:24,695
- [Tom] I'm wearing my magic
rain cape and ski gloves.

2587
01:25:24,695 --> 01:25:26,495
- After all, Star Wolf,

2588
01:25:26,495 --> 01:25:28,375
I'm the one who created you.

2589
01:25:28,375 --> 01:25:30,864
Everything you are and
everything you know,

2590
01:25:30,864 --> 01:25:32,197
you learned from me.
- Yeah, yeah.

2591
01:25:32,197 --> 01:25:33,030
- [Joel] Well, everything I learned,

2592
01:25:33,030 --> 01:25:33,885
I learned in kindergarten.

2593
01:25:33,885 --> 01:25:36,306
- [Halkon] The courage
to pull that trigger.

2594
01:25:36,306 --> 01:25:37,556
- You're wrong.

2595
01:25:38,434 --> 01:25:40,994
Everything I learned from you was wrong.

2596
01:25:40,994 --> 01:25:42,754
- [Joel] Like three-card monte.

2597
01:25:42,754 --> 01:25:44,163
- Was evil.

2598
01:25:44,163 --> 01:25:45,386
Evil.
- Evil.

2599
01:25:45,386 --> 01:25:46,965
- Now I've seen another way of life.

2600
01:25:46,965 --> 01:25:48,453
A life that's honest and decent.

2601
01:25:48,453 --> 01:25:49,354
- I'm going to become a nun!

2602
01:25:49,354 --> 01:25:51,943
- And I've come back to
destroy you and your evil!

2603
01:25:51,943 --> 01:25:53,383
- Ness.

2604
01:25:53,383 --> 01:25:54,365
- [Tom] Thing.

2605
01:25:54,365 --> 01:25:55,303
- Now die!

2606
01:25:55,303 --> 01:25:56,794
- No, you're the one that's gonna die!

2607
01:25:56,794 --> 01:25:57,794
- [Tom] No, you're the
one who's gonna die!

2608
01:25:57,794 --> 01:25:59,312
No, it's you! No, you're
the one who's gonna!

2609
01:25:59,312 --> 01:26:00,394
Who's gonna die?

2610
01:26:00,394 --> 01:26:03,045
(grunts)

2611
01:26:03,045 --> 01:26:05,194
- [Joel] Maybe I am gonna die.

2612
01:26:05,194 --> 01:26:06,111
- Hi-keeba.

2613
01:26:08,994 --> 01:26:12,405
- [Tom] Now I want you
to sing like Tommy Tune.

2614
01:26:12,405 --> 01:26:14,912
(Crow mimics whimpering puppy)

2615
01:26:14,912 --> 01:26:16,525
- [Underling] Lord Halkon!

2616
01:26:16,525 --> 01:26:17,605
Bacchus!

2617
01:26:17,605 --> 01:26:20,483
Bacchus 3 is headed
straight for our fortress!

2618
01:26:20,483 --> 01:26:22,513
(lasers fire)

2619
01:26:22,513 --> 01:26:23,514
- [Tom] Boy, I'll say.

2620
01:26:23,514 --> 01:26:25,165
- [Joel] Kinda looks like Captain Joe's

2621
01:26:25,165 --> 01:26:26,237
in the bucket, you know?

2622
01:26:26,237 --> 01:26:27,717
- [Tom] Yep, yep, yep.

2623
01:26:27,717 --> 01:26:29,125
- Yeah, he's had a few.

2624
01:26:29,125 --> 01:26:31,597
- [Joel] It's the opening of Mannix.

2625
01:26:31,597 --> 01:26:32,430
- Sorry.

2626
01:26:33,935 --> 01:26:37,906
(Tom sings along with score)

2627
01:26:37,906 --> 01:26:40,156
(grunting)

2628
01:26:42,287 --> 01:26:43,416
- [Tom] That was convenient.

2629
01:26:43,416 --> 01:26:45,336
(struggling)

2630
01:26:45,336 --> 01:26:47,034
(grunting)

2631
01:26:47,034 --> 01:26:50,117
(Tom grunting along)

2632
01:26:51,674 --> 01:26:52,924
That's a good defensive move.

2633
01:26:52,924 --> 01:26:54,743
Somersaults.

2634
01:26:54,743 --> 01:26:57,063
(grunting)

2635
01:26:57,063 --> 01:26:58,594
- Ah-ha.

2636
01:26:58,594 --> 01:27:01,602
- Classic Mannix disarm.
- Halkon.

2637
01:27:01,602 --> 01:27:03,052
- Jackie Chan, he is not.

2638
01:27:03,052 --> 01:27:05,302
- Wait a minute, Star Wolf.

2639
01:27:06,412 --> 01:27:07,951
Why don't we discuss this?

2640
01:27:07,951 --> 01:27:10,711
- [Tom] Over a cocktail and some calamari.

2641
01:27:10,711 --> 01:27:12,391
- Put down that sword.

2642
01:27:12,391 --> 01:27:14,362
What's the good of killing me?

2643
01:27:14,362 --> 01:27:16,772
We can be allies. (chuckles)

2644
01:27:16,772 --> 01:27:19,762
(grunting)

2645
01:27:19,762 --> 01:27:21,212
- [Joel] My nut!
(explosion booms)

2646
01:27:21,212 --> 01:27:23,580
(grunting)

2647
01:27:23,580 --> 01:27:26,151
- [Tom] Ooh, big mistake.

2648
01:27:26,151 --> 01:27:27,631
- [Joel] You're dumber
than I thought, Ken.

2649
01:27:27,631 --> 01:27:30,812
(urgent music)

2650
01:27:30,812 --> 01:27:32,229
- Die, Star Wolf!

2651
01:27:33,391 --> 01:27:34,740
(fake mother grunts)
- [Tom] Oh, another one.

2652
01:27:34,740 --> 01:27:37,820
You know, women just shouldn't
hang around this guy.

2653
01:27:37,820 --> 01:27:41,090
- Mother!
- Thanks, substitute mom.

2654
01:27:41,090 --> 01:27:42,257
- Ken, listen.

2655
01:27:43,300 --> 01:27:44,868
I'm not your real mother--

2656
01:27:44,868 --> 01:27:48,268
- [Joel] But an incredible simulation.

2657
01:27:48,268 --> 01:27:49,616
- She's his sister.
- Don't die!

2658
01:27:49,616 --> 01:27:50,616
- [Joe] Ken!

2659
01:27:52,856 --> 01:27:55,727
- Hey, neat, where'd you
get the girl on a stick?

2660
01:27:55,727 --> 01:27:57,235
- [Joe] This must be Halkon's work.

2661
01:27:57,235 --> 01:27:59,750
- [Tom] Yes, notice the fine
detail, the craftsmanship.

2662
01:27:59,750 --> 01:28:01,174
- Look!

2663
01:28:01,174 --> 01:28:02,692
Halkon's getting away.

2664
01:28:02,692 --> 01:28:03,544
- No!

2665
01:28:03,544 --> 01:28:04,412
- [Joel And Bots] Yes!

2666
01:28:04,412 --> 01:28:05,555
- No, he's not!

2667
01:28:05,555 --> 01:28:08,138
(engine booms)

2668
01:28:09,523 --> 01:28:12,254
♪ Super car ♪

2669
01:28:12,254 --> 01:28:13,915
♪ Super car ♪

2670
01:28:13,915 --> 01:28:14,748
- This is it!

2671
01:28:14,748 --> 01:28:15,904
- [Tom] This is it, the night of nights.

2672
01:28:15,904 --> 01:28:18,043
No more rehearsing and nursing our parts.

2673
01:28:18,043 --> 01:28:20,853
(lasers fire)

2674
01:28:20,853 --> 01:28:24,475
- Oop, sorry.
(explosion booms)

2675
01:28:24,475 --> 01:28:26,923
- [Joel] Uh, this is Bernard
Shaw in downtown Bagtown.

2676
01:28:26,923 --> 01:28:29,755
I'm under a table, I'm ready, cam B.

2677
01:28:29,755 --> 01:28:32,443
- [Tom] No, that was George Bernard Shaw.

2678
01:28:32,443 --> 01:28:33,734
- [Joel] In Baghdad?

2679
01:28:33,734 --> 01:28:34,984
- [Tom] No, no.

2680
01:28:36,083 --> 01:28:38,237
So, uh, why do you think they're fighting

2681
01:28:38,237 --> 01:28:39,737
over a Heidelberg?

2682
01:28:40,726 --> 01:28:41,559
(grunting)

2683
01:28:41,559 --> 01:28:43,476
- [Joel] He's gotta go bad, that one.

2684
01:28:43,476 --> 01:28:45,133
- Puppet ships to the rescue!

2685
01:28:45,133 --> 01:28:50,133
(Tom sings theme)
(explosions boom)

2686
01:28:50,173 --> 01:28:53,578
♪ Tried to kill us with a forklift ♪

2687
01:28:53,578 --> 01:28:54,578
- [Tom] Woo!

2688
01:28:55,544 --> 01:28:57,144
- [Joel] Where have I seen this before?

2689
01:28:57,144 --> 01:28:58,211
- [Tom] Oh, I don't know.

2690
01:28:58,211 --> 01:29:00,184
Long time ago in a galaxy far, far away?

2691
01:29:00,184 --> 01:29:02,162
- [Joel] Yup, that's it.

2692
01:29:02,162 --> 01:29:03,829
- [Tom] Pretty much.

2693
01:29:04,882 --> 01:29:05,773
- Attack.

2694
01:29:05,773 --> 01:29:06,864
- [Tom] Oh, he's urging himself on.

2695
01:29:06,864 --> 01:29:08,197
Self-motivation.

2696
01:29:11,464 --> 01:29:12,533
- Now, die!

2697
01:29:12,533 --> 01:29:14,366
- [Joel] You die, Joe!

2698
01:29:20,248 --> 01:29:22,709
- [Halkon] You'll never
destroy me, Star Wolf.

2699
01:29:22,709 --> 01:29:24,989
- You can't destroy me, I quit!

2700
01:29:24,989 --> 01:29:26,176
(explosion booms)

2701
01:29:26,176 --> 01:29:28,265
- [Tom] Oh, well, this has
at least gotta slow it down.

2702
01:29:28,265 --> 01:29:30,197
I mean, please.

2703
01:29:30,197 --> 01:29:31,568
- Put a chink in his get along.

2704
01:29:31,568 --> 01:29:32,707
- [Joel] There goes old Maine.

2705
01:29:32,707 --> 01:29:35,197
The whole campus is gone now.

2706
01:29:35,197 --> 01:29:36,030
- Woo.

2707
01:29:36,030 --> 01:29:37,475
- [Tom] Chink in his get along?

2708
01:29:37,475 --> 01:29:40,475
(takes deep breath)

2709
01:29:42,664 --> 01:29:44,544
- Are you glad we're heading for earth?

2710
01:29:44,544 --> 01:29:45,385
- Yeah.

2711
01:29:45,385 --> 01:29:47,139
- [Crow] 'Cause they have dentists there.

2712
01:29:47,139 --> 01:29:49,200
- There's a girl I can hardly wait to see!

2713
01:29:49,200 --> 01:29:51,320
- [Joel] A girl, you switch-hitter, you.

2714
01:29:51,320 --> 01:29:53,248
- What's wrong with you, Ken?

2715
01:29:53,248 --> 01:29:57,989
I would have thought you'd be
a little more enthusiastic.

2716
01:29:57,989 --> 01:29:59,240
- Captain.

2717
01:29:59,240 --> 01:30:00,109
- [Tom] Gang.

2718
01:30:00,109 --> 01:30:01,400
- I've got something to tell you.

2719
01:30:01,400 --> 01:30:02,468
- [Tom] I want to be a woman.

2720
01:30:02,468 --> 01:30:04,400
- You guys--
- What?

2721
01:30:04,400 --> 01:30:05,408
- [Tom] No, no, no, no.

2722
01:30:05,408 --> 01:30:06,888
- It was great knowing you.

2723
01:30:06,888 --> 01:30:08,166
- It was?

2724
01:30:08,166 --> 01:30:09,549
- [Ken] I've gotta go back to Valna.

2725
01:30:09,549 --> 01:30:11,017
- [Joel] Yeah, we hear your theme song.

2726
01:30:11,017 --> 01:30:11,850
- Ken!

2727
01:30:13,589 --> 01:30:15,549
- What do you hope to accomplish there?

2728
01:30:15,549 --> 01:30:17,219
- [Tom] Well, he signed up
for a health club membership,

2729
01:30:17,219 --> 01:30:18,408
and should use the rest of it.

2730
01:30:18,408 --> 01:30:20,459
It was 18 months.
- The land destroyed.

2731
01:30:20,459 --> 01:30:23,017
- Perhaps I can help
build a new nation there.

2732
01:30:23,017 --> 01:30:24,320
A new civilization.

2733
01:30:24,320 --> 01:30:27,909
- So you think you can
change the world, do ya?

2734
01:30:27,909 --> 01:30:29,379
- That's an impossible job.

2735
01:30:29,379 --> 01:30:31,168
- You'd need 10 lifetimes to complete it.

2736
01:30:31,168 --> 01:30:32,208
Think it over!

2737
01:30:32,208 --> 01:30:34,240
- Why don't you just stick with us, Ken?

2738
01:30:34,240 --> 01:30:36,978
After all, you started
life as an Earthling.

2739
01:30:36,978 --> 01:30:37,811
- [Joel] Yeah, I'll get help.

2740
01:30:37,811 --> 01:30:40,339
Maybe some hire some staff, I dunno.

2741
01:30:40,339 --> 01:30:41,549
- And died there.

2742
01:30:41,549 --> 01:30:44,218
I want to finish their work.

2743
01:30:44,218 --> 01:30:45,520
- Well, it's not exactly on our way.

2744
01:30:45,520 --> 01:30:47,280
- [Joe] It's your decision.

2745
01:30:47,280 --> 01:30:49,376
- [Tom] Boy, his cheeks are huge.

2746
01:30:49,376 --> 01:30:50,320
- Good luck, Ken.

2747
01:30:50,320 --> 01:30:51,429
Star Wolf.

2748
01:30:51,429 --> 01:30:52,888
- [Joel] Thanks, I think.

2749
01:30:52,888 --> 01:30:55,717
(reverent music)

2750
01:30:55,717 --> 01:30:57,179
- I'll just shake your hand.

2751
01:30:57,179 --> 01:30:58,589
- But I won't kiss you.

2752
01:30:58,589 --> 01:31:02,922
- I don't like goodbyes.
(Tom sobs)

2753
01:31:04,448 --> 01:31:07,031
- Billy.
- Don't be a hero, man.

2754
01:31:08,168 --> 01:31:10,307
- It's been great.
- Thanks.

2755
01:31:10,307 --> 01:31:11,140
- Dan?

2756
01:31:11,140 --> 01:31:13,248
- [Tom] Or whatever your name is, new guy.

2757
01:31:13,248 --> 01:31:14,081
I think I woulda liked you.

2758
01:31:14,081 --> 01:31:15,197
- We been through a lot together.

2759
01:31:15,197 --> 01:31:17,030
- Yeah.
- Soul brother.

2760
01:31:18,356 --> 01:31:19,189
- Tammy?

2761
01:31:20,099 --> 01:31:21,659
I'll never forget you.

2762
01:31:21,659 --> 01:31:24,067
- [Tom] And I'll never forget you, um, uh,

2763
01:31:24,067 --> 01:31:24,900
oh, Ken.

2764
01:31:25,947 --> 01:31:27,280
Ooh, doll hands.

2765
01:31:28,616 --> 01:31:29,783
- Ah, grow up.

2766
01:31:30,888 --> 01:31:33,496
- [Joel] Hey, they're gonna
land on that bowling ball.

2767
01:31:33,496 --> 01:31:35,886
(Tom sings along with score)
(instruments beep)

2768
01:31:35,886 --> 01:31:36,937
(clicking)

2769
01:31:36,937 --> 01:31:38,697
- Ready now. Take off!

2770
01:31:38,697 --> 01:31:39,708
- Take off, hoser!

2771
01:31:39,708 --> 01:31:40,708
- [Tom] Woo!

2772
01:31:46,228 --> 01:31:47,927
(Tom yelps)

2773
01:31:47,927 --> 01:31:49,897
(Tom sings along with store)

2774
01:31:49,897 --> 01:31:52,137
- Goodbye, Star Wolf.

2775
01:31:52,137 --> 01:31:56,147
- Goodbye, Ken.
- Goodnight, sweet prince.

2776
01:31:56,147 --> 01:31:57,087
- [Joel] Oh, look at that suit.

2777
01:31:57,087 --> 01:31:59,016
What, is he going to be in
swing choir or something?

2778
01:31:59,016 --> 01:32:01,308
(Tom chuckles)

2779
01:32:01,308 --> 01:32:02,948
- And we have closure.

2780
01:32:02,948 --> 01:32:04,257
- Yay!
- Woo!

2781
01:32:04,257 --> 01:32:06,359
- [Tom] Woo woo woo!
(Crow whistles)

2782
01:32:06,359 --> 01:32:09,495
Fugitive Alien will be back
in Fugitive Alien Come Home,

2783
01:32:09,495 --> 01:32:11,128
Fugitive Alien III,

2784
01:32:11,128 --> 01:32:14,295
The Next Day, The Final Chapter, 3000.

2785
01:32:27,345 --> 01:32:30,056
- Uh, let's see here,
uh, Brewster's Millions.

2786
01:32:30,056 --> 01:32:31,425
Uh, Brian's Song.

2787
01:32:31,425 --> 01:32:33,885
- Oh, no, no, I couldn't handle
Brian's Song again, Crow.

2788
01:32:33,885 --> 01:32:35,925
When I saw that, I was
dewy-eyed for a week.

2789
01:32:35,925 --> 01:32:37,477
- Oh, it didn't effect me that way at all.

2790
01:32:37,477 --> 01:32:38,485
